#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.after"
msgid "A decision you, or the world, settled says what happened to it rather than leaving."
msgstr "Una decisión que resolviste tú, o que resolvió el mundo, muestra cómo terminó en lugar de desaparecer."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.answer"
msgid "Alerts tell you what happened and what needs you; the game always shows them, and this device can too."
msgstr "Los avisos te dicen qué pasó y qué necesita de ti; el juego siempre los muestra, y este dispositivo también puede hacerlo."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.line"
msgid "What you are told, and where."
msgstr "Qué se te avisa y dónde."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step1.how"
msgid "open Alerts from Home: Waiting on you first, then Important, then the rest by day."
msgstr "abre Avisos desde Inicio: primero Te esperan, luego Importante y después el resto, por día."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step1.to"
msgid "To read them"
msgstr "Para leerlos"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step2.how"
msgid "press it: it opens the thing itself, and Back returns to the list."
msgstr "púlsalo y se abre lo que anuncia; Atrás vuelve a la lista."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step2.to"
msgid "To act on one"
msgstr "Para actuar sobre uno"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step3.how"
msgid "open Settings, then Alerts, turn on alerts on this device, and choose which kinds reach it."
msgstr "abre Ajustes, luego Avisos, activa los avisos en este dispositivo y elige qué tipos te llegan."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step3.to"
msgid "To get them on this device"
msgstr "Para recibirlos en este dispositivo"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.synonyms"
msgid "alert, notification, notify, push, phone, news"
msgstr "aviso, avisos, alerta, alertas, notificación, notificacion, notificaciones, notificar, push, teléfono, telefono, noticias"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.title"
msgid "How alerts work"
msgstr "Cómo funcionan los avisos"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.word1.means"
msgid "News that changes your country or your things, such as a war."
msgstr "Noticias que afectan a tu país o a lo tuyo, como una guerra."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.word1.term"
msgid "Important"
msgstr "Importante"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.line"
msgid "Votes on every bill, and may propose one."
msgstr "Vota todos los proyectos de ley y puede proponer uno."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p1"
msgid "<b>A member votes on every bill before the chamber, and may propose bills.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Un miembro vota todos los proyectos de ley que llegan a la cámara y puede proponer proyectos.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p2"
msgid "Seats are elected by place: a member stands for where their voters live, for the term the constitution sets."
msgstr "Los escaños se eligen por lugar: un miembro representa el sitio donde viven sus votantes, durante el mandato que fija la constitución."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p3"
msgid "To vote: the seat’s console under You lists each bill waiting on your vote, with its tally and when it closes."
msgstr "Para votar: la consola del escaño, en Tú, lista cada proyecto de ley que espera tu voto, con su recuento y cuándo cierra."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p4"
msgid "Your votes are public, and the console keeps them: every bill you voted on, and how it ended."
msgstr "Tus votos son públicos y la consola los guarda: cada proyecto de ley que votaste y cómo terminó."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.title"
msgid "What does a member of the Assembly do?"
msgstr "¿Qué hace un miembro de la Asamblea?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.line"
msgid "What it takes, and what is spent."
msgstr "Qué hace falta y qué se gasta."

#. {level} is a player level. {charter} is the charter fee, drawn as a coin amount. {capital} is the least capital, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.p1"
msgid "From level {level} you can found a bank from You › Start something. It takes a {charter} charter fee, which is spent, and at least {capital} of your own money, which becomes the bank’s cash."
msgstr "Desde el nivel {level} puedes fundar un banco desde Tú › Crear algo. Cuesta una tasa de licencia de {charter}, que se gasta, y al menos {capital} de tu propio dinero, que pasa a ser el efectivo del banco."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.p2"
msgid "A bank can fail, and the people who bank there can lose money. You can wind a bank up, but founding one cannot be undone."
msgstr "Un banco puede quebrar, y quienes guardan allí su dinero pueden perderlo. Puedes liquidar un banco, pero fundarlo no se puede deshacer."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.title"
msgid "How do I start a bank?"
msgstr "¿Cómo fundo un banco?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.li1"
msgid "<b>What it lends on:</b> published terms. Anyone who fits them borrows without asking you. You can change them, or take them down; loans already made stay as they are."
msgstr "<b>En qué condiciones presta:</b> condiciones publicadas. Cualquiera que las cumpla pide prestado sin pedirte permiso. Puedes cambiarlas o retirarlas; los préstamos ya concedidos quedan como están."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.li2"
msgid "<b>Offer someone a loan:</b> the money leaves the bank only when they accept. One offer at a time to one person; you can withdraw it while it waits."
msgstr "<b>Ofrecer un préstamo a alguien:</b> el dinero sale del banco solo cuando esa persona acepta. Una oferta a la vez para una persona; puedes retirarla mientras espera."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.li3"
msgid "<b>Who owes it money:</b> each loan and how it is going. A loan nobody repays is a loss nothing makes good."
msgstr "<b>Quién le debe dinero:</b> cada préstamo y cómo va. Un préstamo que nadie devuelve es una pérdida que nada compensa."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.line"
msgid "Whether it can pay out, who owes it, and its terms."
msgstr "Si puede pagar, quién le debe y sus condiciones."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.p1"
msgid "A bank keeps other players’ money and lends it. Its console says first whether it <b>can pay out</b>: its cash against what it owes the people who bank there."
msgstr "Un banco guarda el dinero de otros jugadores y lo presta. Su consola dice primero si <b>puede pagar</b>: su efectivo frente a lo que debe a quienes guardan allí su dinero."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.p2"
msgid "A bank that owes depositors more than it holds says so first. Winding a bank up is at the foot of More options and cannot be undone."
msgstr "Un banco que debe a sus depositantes más de lo que tiene lo dice primero. Liquidar un banco está al final de Más opciones y no se puede deshacer."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.title"
msgid "Running a bank"
msgstr "Dirigir un banco"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.line"
msgid "Keep money in a bank, borrow it, or run a bank yourself."
msgstr "Guarda dinero en un banco, pídelo prestado o dirige tú un banco."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p1"
msgid "<b>Banks are run by players: you can put money in one, or borrow from one that lends to you.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Los bancos los dirigen los jugadores: puedes poner dinero en uno o pedir un préstamo a uno que te lo ofrezca.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p2"
msgid "To put money in: open Money, then Banks, and press Put money in on a bank. No bank pays interest on it. You take it out when the bank has the money to pay you."
msgstr "Para poner dinero: abre Dinero, luego Bancos, y pulsa Poner dinero en un banco. Ningún banco paga intereses por él. Lo retiras cuando el banco tiene dinero para pagarte."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p3"
msgid "To borrow: open Money, then Loans. Each bank says how much it lends, its interest a year, for how long and how often you pay. The Borrow sheet says each payment, the day of the last, and what a missed payment does under that bank’s terms. One loan per bank at a time."
msgstr "Para pedir un préstamo: abre Dinero, luego Préstamos. Cada banco indica cuánto presta, su interés anual, por cuánto tiempo y cada cuánto pagas. El panel de Pedir prestado indica cada cuota, el día de la última y qué ocurre si no pagas una cuota según las condiciones de ese banco. Un préstamo por banco a la vez."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p4"
msgid "To pay it back early: open the loan and press Repay, or Repay it all."
msgstr "Para devolverlo antes de tiempo: abre el préstamo y pulsa Devolver o Devolver todo."

#. {level} is a player level. {charter} is the charter fee, drawn as a coin amount. {capital} is the least capital, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p5"
msgid "From Level {level} you can found a bank: {charter} for the charter and at least {capital} of capital."
msgstr "Desde el nivel {level} puedes fundar un banco: {charter} de licencia y al menos {capital} de capital."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p6"
msgid "Words: Deposit: money you put in a bank. Interest: what a loan costs a year, as a part of what you borrow."
msgstr "Palabras: Depósito: dinero que pones en un banco. Interés: lo que cuesta un préstamo al año, como una parte de lo que pides prestado."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.title"
msgid "How do banks and loans work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan los bancos y los préstamos?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.answer"
msgid "Work your first shift, eat, train and choose where you live; Getting started in Now walks you through it."
msgstr "Trabaja tu primer turno, come, entrena y elige dónde vivir; Primeros pasos, en Ahora, te guía paso a paso."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.line"
msgid "What to do first, step by step."
msgstr "Qué hacer primero, paso a paso."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {food} is a number of food items. {starterGrant} is the money a new citizen starts with, drawn as a coin amount. {newCountryGrant} is the money a newcomer starts with in a country that is still new, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step1.how"
msgid "you are a citizen already, with {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} in a country that is still new), {food} food and a basic set of gear."
msgstr "ya eres ciudadano, con {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} en un país que aún es nuevo), {food} unidades de comida y un equipo básico."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step1.to"
msgid "To begin"
msgstr "Para empezar"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step2.how"
msgid "press Work a shift on Home. Public works take anyone, with or without a job."
msgstr "pulsa Trabajar un turno en Inicio. Las obras públicas aceptan a cualquiera, con o sin empleo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step2.to"
msgid "To earn"
msgstr "Para ganar dinero"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step3.how"
msgid "train once a day and finish today's goals; each level opens more of the game."
msgstr "entrena una vez al día y termina los objetivos de hoy; cada nivel abre más partes del juego."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step3.to"
msgid "To grow"
msgstr "Para crecer"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step4.how"
msgid "open a province on the map and choose Live here once you stand in it."
msgstr "abre una provincia en el mapa y elige Vivir aquí cuando estés en ella."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step4.to"
msgid "To settle"
msgstr "Para instalarte"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step5.how"
msgid "vote after a few days, trade on the Market, write for a paper, and fight when your country is at war."
msgstr "vota pasados unos días, comercia en el Mercado, escribe para un periódico y combate cuando tu país esté en guerra."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step5.to"
msgid "Later"
msgstr "Más adelante"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.synonyms"
msgid "new, start, begin, first, tutorial, guide, how to play"
msgstr "nuevo, nueva, empezar, comenzar, inicio, primeros pasos, primer día, tutorial, guía, guia, cómo jugar, como jugar, principiante, ayuda"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.title"
msgid "Your first hour"
msgstr "Tu primera hora"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word1.means"
msgid "The steps in Now that take you through your first day."
msgstr "Los pasos de Ahora que te guían durante tu primer día."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word1.term"
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Primeros pasos"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word2.means"
msgid "What your experience adds up to; each one opens more of the game."
msgstr "Lo que suma tu experiencia; cada uno abre más partes del juego."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word2.term"
msgid "Level"
msgstr "Nivel"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.line"
msgid "Members propose bills and vote on them."
msgstr "Los miembros proponen proyectos de ley y los votan."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p1"
msgid "<b>The chamber is the country’s elected assembly. Its members propose bills and vote on each for {hours} hours.</b>"
msgstr "<b>La cámara es la asamblea elegida del país. Sus miembros proponen proyectos de ley y votan cada uno durante {hours} horas.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p2"
msgid "A bill passes with more yes than no votes. A change to the constitution needs two thirds. How each member voted is public."
msgstr "Un proyecto de ley se aprueba con más votos a favor que en contra. Un cambio a la constitución necesita dos tercios. El voto de cada miembro es público."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p3"
msgid "To follow a bill: Country, Politics, The chamber lists every bill, its tally and when its vote closes."
msgstr "Para seguir un proyecto de ley: abre País, Política, La cámara, que lista cada proyecto de ley, su recuento y cuándo cierra su votación."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p4"
msgid "To propose one: a member, or an office that may propose bills, uses Propose a bill on the same screen."
msgstr "Para proponer uno: un miembro, o un cargo que pueda proponer proyectos de ley, usa Proponer un proyecto de ley en la misma pantalla."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p5"
msgid "Words: Member: somebody holding a seat in the chamber."
msgstr "Palabras: Miembro: alguien que ocupa un escaño en la cámara."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.title"
msgid "How does the chamber work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funciona la cámara?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.line"
msgid "Rooms, direct messages, and staying safe."
msgstr "Salas, mensajes directos y cómo protegerte."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p1"
msgid "<b>Chat is the rooms you are in and the people you write to.</b>"
msgstr "<b>El Chat son las salas en las que estás y las personas a las que escribes.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p2"
msgid "Your rooms: the whole world, your country, and every party, unit, company or battle you belong to. Press a room to open it."
msgstr "Tus salas: el mundo entero, tu país y cada partido, unidad, empresa o batalla a la que perteneces. Pulsa una sala para abrirla."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p3"
msgid "To write: type in the box and press Send. The world room may ask you to wait between messages, and Send counts it down. Press + to mention somebody, add an emoji or a sticker, or attach a picture."
msgstr "Para escribir: escribe en el cuadro y pulsa Enviar. La sala del mundo puede pedirte que esperes entre mensajes, y Enviar cuenta el tiempo. Pulsa + para mencionar a alguien, añadir un emoji o un sticker, o adjuntar una imagen."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p4"
msgid "To answer one message: open its ⋯ and press Reply. To write to one person, press Message on their page."
msgstr "Para responder a un mensaje: abre su ⋯ y pulsa Responder. Para escribir a una persona, pulsa Mensaje en su página."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.title"
msgid "How does Chat work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funciona el Chat?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.line"
msgid "Which country you belong to, and moving to another."
msgstr "A qué país perteneces y cómo pasar a otro."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p1"
msgid "<b>You are a citizen of one country at a time. It is where you vote, run for office and join a party.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Tienes la ciudadanía de un solo país a la vez. En él votas, te presentas a un cargo y te unes a un partido.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p2"
msgid "To change: open the other country’s People and apply. Some countries let everyone in at once; in others an office decides. The application says what moving would end for you."
msgstr "Para cambiar: abre Personas en el otro país y haz tu solicitud. Algunos países admiten a todos de inmediato; en otros decide un cargo. La solicitud dice qué dejarías atrás al mudarte."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p3"
msgid "There is a wait between changes, and after moving you wait longer before you can vote or run. Your own dates are on the People screen."
msgstr "Hay una espera entre cambios, y tras mudarte esperas más antes de poder votar o presentarte. Tus propias fechas están en la pantalla Personas."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p4"
msgid "Words: Citizen: a member of a country."
msgstr "Palabras: Ciudadano: miembro de un país."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.title"
msgid "Citizenship, and how to change it"
msgstr "La ciudadanía y cómo cambiarla"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.line"
msgid "Frames, banners and name colours for how you look."
msgstr "Marcos, banners y colores de nombre para tu aspecto."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p1"
msgid "<b>Coins are a second currency, for how you look and how much room you have, never for an advantage.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Las Monedas son una segunda divisa, para cómo te ves y cuánto espacio tienes, nunca para ganar ventaja.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p2"
msgid "They are bought with real money once the store opens, and buying them is not open yet. They cannot be turned into CR."
msgstr "Se compran con dinero real cuando abra la Tienda, y comprarlas todavía no está disponible. No se pueden convertir en CR."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p3"
msgid "To try something on: open it in the Store and press Try it on. Only you see it, nothing is bought, and it ends when you leave the Store."
msgstr "Para probar algo: ábrelo en la Tienda y pulsa Probar. Solo tú lo ves, no se compra nada y termina cuando sales de la Tienda."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p4"
msgid "To wear what you own: open it and press Wear. A title you earned is worn from your public page."
msgstr "Para ponerte lo que tienes: ábrelo y pulsa Ponerse. Un título que ganaste se lleva desde tu página pública."

#. {coins} is a number of Coins.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p5"
msgid "Supporter, once it is on sale: {coins} Coins a month, a badge and extra slots. The tip jar on Ko-fi buys nothing and changes nothing."
msgstr "Mecenas, cuando esté a la venta: {coins} Monedas al mes, una insignia y espacios extra. El bote de propinas de Ko-fi no compra nada ni cambia nada."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p6"
msgid "Words: Coins: the Store’s currency. Supporter: a monthly subscription for looks and room."
msgstr "Palabras: Monedas: la divisa de la Tienda. Mecenas: una suscripción mensual para el aspecto y el espacio."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.title"
msgid "What are Coins?"
msgstr "¿Qué son las Monedas?"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.h1"
msgid "Words"
msgstr "Palabras"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li1"
msgid "<b>To make something:</b> open a site. It is a building in a province of your company’s country. The price shown is the whole price: the building and the goods bought for it."
msgstr "<b>Para fabricar algo:</b> abre una instalación. Es un edificio en una provincia del país de tu empresa. El precio que se muestra es el precio total: el edificio y los bienes comprados para él."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li2"
msgid "<b>To get it working:</b> advertise for people under People. Both sides are held for 24 hours once somebody is hired."
msgstr "<b>Para ponerla a funcionar:</b> anuncia puestos en Personas. Ambas partes quedan vinculadas durante 24 horas cuando se contrata a alguien."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li3"
msgid "<b>To sell what it makes:</b> Trade and stock opens the Market as the company."
msgstr "<b>Para vender lo que produce:</b> Comercio y existencias abre el Mercado como la empresa."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li4"
msgid "<b>To pay its owners:</b> Money. It keeps two weeks of wages and what it owes."
msgstr "<b>Para pagar a sus propietarios:</b> Dinero. La empresa conserva dos semanas de salarios y lo que debe."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.line"
msgid "Sites, people, money and stock, from one screen."
msgstr "Instalaciones, personas, dinero y existencias, desde una sola pantalla."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.p1"
msgid "Open it from You: its first screen says what waits on you, what is wrong, and what runs by itself."
msgstr "Ábrela desde Tú: su primera pantalla dice qué te espera, qué va mal y qué funciona solo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.p2"
msgid "<b>Site:</b> a building where your company makes things. <b>Stock:</b> what its sites hold. <b>Payout:</b> money paid to its owners by their shares."
msgstr "<b>Instalación:</b> un edificio donde tu empresa fabrica cosas. <b>Existencias:</b> lo que guardan sus instalaciones. <b>Reparto:</b> dinero que se paga a sus propietarios según sus acciones."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.title"
msgid "How do I run a company?"
msgstr "¿Cómo dirijo una empresa?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.li1"
msgid "<b>Alone:</b> you pay all of it and own all of it."
msgstr "<b>En solitario:</b> lo pagas todo tú y todo es tuyo."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label. {partners} is a number of citizens. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.li2"
msgid "<b>With partners:</b> up to {partners} citizens of its country put money in and own shares by what they put in. You send them a link. If it is not all in within {hours} hours, everyone’s money goes back."
msgstr "<b>Con socios:</b> hasta {partners} ciudadanos de su país ponen dinero y poseen acciones según lo que aportan. Tú les envías un enlace. Si no está todo aportado en {hours} horas, el dinero de todos se devuelve."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.li3"
msgid "<b>Where it is registered is for good:</b> it can only build in that country. The fee goes to the treasury of whoever holds the province."
msgstr "<b>El país donde se registra es para siempre:</b> solo puede construir en ese país. La tasa va al tesoro público de quien tenga la provincia."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.line"
msgid "Alone or with partners, and what is for good."
msgstr "En solitario o con socios, y qué es para siempre."

#. {level} is a player level. {charter} is the fee to found a company, drawn as a coin amount. {startMoney} is the least start money a company needs, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.p1"
msgid "From level {level} you can found a company from You › Start something. It takes a {charter} fee and at least {startMoney} of start money, which becomes the company’s."
msgstr "Desde el nivel {level} puedes fundar una empresa desde Tú › Crear algo. Cuesta una tasa de {charter} y al menos {startMoney} de dinero inicial, que pasa a ser de la empresa."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.p2"
msgid "Once it exists, open its first site: until then it can make and hire nothing."
msgstr "Cuando exista, abre su primera instalación: hasta entonces no puede fabricar ni contratar nada."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.title"
msgid "How do I start a company?"
msgstr "¿Cómo fundo una empresa?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li1"
msgid "<b>Advertise for people:</b> say how many, from which level, and the pay for a short shift. The screen says what a full shift then pays, and warns you when you would pay more than a shift makes."
msgstr "<b>Anunciar puestos:</b> indica cuántas personas, desde qué nivel y el pago por un turno corto. La pantalla indica cuánto paga entonces un turno completo y te avisa cuando pagarías más de lo que produce un turno."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li2"
msgid "<b>Ask me first</b> lets you answer each person. <b>Hire anyone who qualifies</b> takes them at once."
msgstr "<b>Pregúntame antes</b> te deja responder a cada persona. <b>Contratar a cualquiera que cumpla los requisitos</b> contrata a cada persona al instante."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li3"
msgid "<b>Answering:</b> Hire or Refuse. Once somebody is hired, both sides are held for {hours} hours."
msgstr "<b>Responder:</b> Contratar o Rechazar. Cuando se contrata a alguien, ambas partes quedan vinculadas durante {hours} horas."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li4"
msgid "<b>Wages</b> are paid from the company’s money each day; the console says how many days it has in hand."
msgstr "<b>Los salarios</b> se pagan cada día con el dinero de la empresa; la consola dice para cuántos días alcanza."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.line"
msgid "Adverts, applicants, pay, and handing hiring over."
msgstr "Anuncios, solicitantes, pago y cómo delegar la contratación."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.p1"
msgid "A company hires from its People once it has a site that is open."
msgstr "Una empresa contrata desde su sección Personas cuando tiene una instalación abierta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.p2"
msgid "Under More options you can let idle workers go after a number of days, or hand hiring over to someone you trust, with a job title."
msgstr "En Más opciones puedes despedir a quienes llevan inactivos cierto número de días, o delegar la contratación en alguien de confianza, con un título de puesto."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.title"
msgid "How do I hire people?"
msgstr "¿Cómo contrato personas?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li1"
msgid "<b>What it makes:</b> each choice shows the whole price of its cheapest place, what a site makes a day and what that sells for today."
msgstr "<b>Qué produce:</b> cada opción muestra el precio total de su lugar más barato, lo que produce una instalación al día y por cuánto se vende hoy."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li2"
msgid "<b>Where:</b> a province of your company’s own country, with its industry level and the room left. A province another country holds is shown, and cannot be chosen."
msgstr "<b>Dónde:</b> una provincia del propio país de tu empresa, con su nivel industrial y el espacio que queda. Una provincia en manos de otro país se muestra, pero no se puede elegir."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li3"
msgid "<b>How big:</b> a bigger site has more places to work. You can make it bigger later; it stops for a few hours then."
msgstr "<b>De qué tamaño:</b> una instalación más grande tiene más puestos de trabajo. Puedes ampliarla después; entonces se detiene unas horas."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li4"
msgid "<b>The price:</b> the building and the goods it needs, bought on the Market for the company. Nothing more is spent than the price you were shown."
msgstr "<b>El precio:</b> el edificio y los bienes que necesita, comprados en el Mercado para la empresa. No se gasta nada más que el precio que viste."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.line"
msgid "What it makes, where, how big, and what it costs."
msgstr "Qué produce, dónde, de qué tamaño y cuánto cuesta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.p1"
msgid "A site is a building where your company makes one thing. Open one from your company’s Sites."
msgstr "Una instalación es un edificio donde tu empresa produce una sola cosa. Abre una desde las Instalaciones de tu empresa."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.p2"
msgid "A site works once it has people, or an automation line. Pulling one down is at the foot of the site’s More options."
msgstr "Una instalación funciona cuando tiene personas o una línea de automatización. Derribarla está al final de Más opciones de la instalación."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.title"
msgid "How do I open a site?"
msgstr "¿Cómo abro una instalación?"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.h1"
msgid "Voting and running for office"
msgstr "Votar y presentarse a un cargo"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.h2"
msgid "Laws and taxes"
msgstr "Leyes e impuestos"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.h3"
msgid "Changing citizenship and parties"
msgstr "Cambiar de ciudadanía y de partido"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.line"
msgid "Citizenship, elections, laws and taxes."
msgstr "Ciudadanía, elecciones, leyes e impuestos."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p1"
msgid "Every country is run by its players. Citizens elect the people who make the laws, set the taxes and can declare war."
msgstr "Cada país lo dirigen sus jugadores. Los ciudadanos eligen a quienes hacen las leyes, fijan los impuestos y pueden declarar la guerra."

#. The first three numbers are days of citizenship: {originalVote} before voting, {originalAssembly} before running for the assembly, {originalHeadOfState} before running for head of state, for a citizen who never changed country. {migrantVote}, {migrantAssembly} and {migrantHeadOfState} are the same three waits, in days, for a citizen who moved from another country.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p2"
msgid "Both depend on how many days you have been a citizen of that country. If you have never changed citizenship, you can vote after {originalVote} days, run for the assembly after {originalAssembly} and for head of state after {originalHeadOfState}. If you moved from another country it is {migrantVote}, {migrantAssembly} and {migrantHeadOfState} days. The Country screen shows your own dates."
msgstr "Ambas cosas dependen de cuántos días llevas con la ciudadanía de ese país. Si nunca has cambiado de ciudadanía, puedes votar tras {originalVote} días, presentarte a la Asamblea tras {originalAssembly} y a la jefatura de Estado tras {originalHeadOfState}. Si viniste de otro país, son {migrantVote}, {migrantAssembly} y {migrantHeadOfState} días. La pantalla País muestra tus propias fechas."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p3"
msgid "While a country is new there is no wait at all: see A new country."
msgstr "Mientras un país es nuevo no hay ninguna espera: consulta Un país nuevo."

#. {nominationDays} is a number of days. {votingDays} is a number of days.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p4"
msgid "An election has {nominationDays} day for candidates to run, then {votingDays} day of voting, the first election for an office too. If nobody runs against you, you take the seat when entries close, with no vote. A chamber is elected by place, so for a seat in it that means nobody else running where you live. An office the chamber chooses, such as a prime minister, is the exception: anybody may run for it, and the chamber’s members always vote, even on one name."
msgstr "Una elección tiene {nominationDays} día para que se presenten los candidatos y luego {votingDays} día de votación, y esto vale también para la primera elección de un cargo. Si nadie se presenta contra ti, te quedas con el puesto cuando se cierran las candidaturas, sin votación. Una cámara se elige por lugar, así que para un escaño en ella eso significa que nadie más se presenta donde vives. Un cargo que elige la cámara, como el de primer ministro, es la excepción: cualquiera puede presentarse a él, y los miembros de la cámara siempre votan, incluso con un solo nombre."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p5"
msgid "Members of the assembly propose laws and vote on them for {hours} hours. A president or prime minister may propose laws too, and votes on them only with a seat of their own. A law passes with more yes than no votes; a change to the constitution needs two thirds. Taxes are set this way, so they differ from country to country: see your country’s Money room."
msgstr "Los miembros de la Asamblea proponen leyes y las votan durante {hours} horas. Quien ocupa la presidencia o el puesto de primer ministro también puede proponer leyes, y vota sobre ellas solo si tiene un escaño propio. Una ley se aprueba con más votos a favor que en contra; un cambio a la constitución necesita dos tercios. Los impuestos se fijan así, por lo que cambian de un país a otro: mira la sección Dinero de tu país."

#. {level} is a player level. {fee} is the fee to found a party, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p6"
msgid "You can apply to become a citizen of another country. Some countries accept everyone at once, others have an official decide. There is a wait between changes. From level {level} you can found a political party for {fee}."
msgstr "Puedes solicitar la ciudadanía de otro país. Algunos países aceptan a todos de inmediato; en otros decide una autoridad. Hay una espera entre cambios. Desde el nivel {level} puedes fundar un partido político por {fee}."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.title"
msgid "Your country and how to take part"
msgstr "Tu país y cómo participar"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.after"
msgid "A new day starts at midnight UTC."
msgstr "Un día nuevo empieza a medianoche UTC."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.answer"
msgid "Work a shift, train and eat, then see what is waiting on you."
msgstr "Trabaja un turno, entrena y come, y luego mira qué te espera."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.line"
msgid "Work, train, eat, and what waits on you."
msgstr "Trabajar, entrenar, comer y lo que te espera."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {shortShift} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step1.how"
msgid "press Work a shift on Home. A short shift costs {shortShift} Energy and pays a wage in CR."
msgstr "pulsa Trabajar un turno en Inicio. Un turno corto cuesta {shortShift} de Energía y paga un salario en CR."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step1.to"
msgid "To earn money"
msgstr "Para ganar dinero"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {training} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step2.how"
msgid "press Train for battle, once a day, for {training} Energy. You hit harder in a battle."
msgstr "pulsa Entrenar para la batalla, una vez al día, por {training} de Energía. Golpeas más fuerte en una batalla."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step2.to"
msgid "To get stronger"
msgstr "Para fortalecerte"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {foodEnergy} is an amount of Energy. {restingEnergy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step3.how"
msgid "press Eat. One food gives {foodEnergy} Energy; on its own, Energy comes back up to {restingEnergy}."
msgstr "pulsa Comer. Una comida da {foodEnergy} de Energía; por sí sola, la Energía se recupera hasta {restingEnergy}."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step3.to"
msgid "To get Energy back"
msgstr "Para recuperar Energía"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step4.how"
msgid "look at Waiting on you at the top of Now. Each line says by when."
msgstr "mira Te esperan, arriba en Ahora. Cada línea dice para cuándo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step4.to"
msgid "To see what needs you"
msgstr "Para ver qué te espera"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {reward} is the reward, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step5.how"
msgid "finish today’s goals for {reward} and a case."
msgstr "termina los objetivos de hoy: recibes {reward} y una caja."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.step5.to"
msgid "To earn a little more"
msgstr "Para ganar un poco más"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.synonyms"
msgid "each day, daily, routine, what now, today"
msgstr "cada día, cada dia, diario, diaria, a diario, rutina, qué hago, que hago, ahora, hoy, día, dia"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.title"
msgid "What do I do each day?"
msgstr "¿Qué hago cada día?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.word1.means"
msgid "What work, training and fighting use."
msgstr "Lo que gastan el trabajo, el entrenamiento y el combate."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.word1.term"
msgid "Energy"
msgstr "Energía"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.word2.means"
msgid "Credits, the game's money."
msgstr "Créditos, el dinero del juego."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.word2.term"
msgid "CR"
msgstr "CR"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.word3.means"
msgid "Decisions only you can make, each with its deadline."
msgstr "Decisiones que solo tú puedes tomar, cada una con su plazo."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.daily.word3.term"
msgid "Waiting on you"
msgstr "Te esperan"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.line"
msgid "Bills, laws and what each office may do."
msgstr "Proyectos de ley, leyes y lo que puede hacer cada cargo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.p1"
msgid "<b>By law. Members of the chamber propose bills and vote on them, and a bill that passes becomes law.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Por ley. Los miembros de la cámara proponen proyectos de ley y los votan, y un proyecto aprobado se convierte en ley.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.p2"
msgid "Some acts belong to an office instead: whoever holds it acts within the powers its page lists, such as spending from the Treasury up to a limit. A power the constitution keeps for the chamber is done by proposing a bill."
msgstr "Algunos actos corresponden en cambio a un cargo: quien lo ocupa actúa dentro de las facultades que lista su página, como gastar del tesoro público hasta un límite. Una facultad que la constitución reserva a la cámara se ejerce proponiendo un proyecto de ley."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.p3"
msgid "Citizens choose who holds the offices and the seats in elections, and can be asked one question in a referendum."
msgstr "Los ciudadanos eligen en elecciones quién ocupa los cargos y los escaños, y se les puede hacer una sola pregunta en un referendo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.p4"
msgid "To take part: vote in Country, Politics, Elections; run for an office there; or ask your member of the chamber to propose a bill."
msgstr "Para participar: vota en País, Política, Elecciones; preséntate allí a un cargo; o pide a tu miembro de la cámara que proponga un proyecto de ley."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.p5"
msgid "Words: Bill: a proposed law. Law: a bill that passed. Power: what an office may do."
msgstr "Palabras: Proyecto de ley: una ley propuesta. Ley: un proyecto de ley aprobado. Facultad: lo que puede hacer un cargo."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.deciding.title"
msgid "How does this country decide things?"
msgstr "¿Cómo decide las cosas este país?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.li1"
msgid "Better transport makes journeys shorter and can give a province an airport."
msgstr "Un mejor transporte acorta los viajes y puede dar un aeropuerto a una provincia."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label. {tierOne} is a number of days. {tierTwo} is a number of days. {tierThree} is a number of days. {floor} is the lowest price, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.li2"
msgid "Research comes in three tiers and helps the whole country. A tier costs {tierOne}, {tierTwo} and {tierThree} days of what the country takes in, never less than {floor}, plus goods. A minister starts it from Country, Economy, or a law orders it."
msgstr "La investigación tiene tres niveles y ayuda a todo el país. Un nivel cuesta {tierOne}, {tierTwo} y {tierThree} días de lo que ingresa el país, nunca menos de {floor}, más bienes. Un ministro la inicia desde País, Economía, o una ley lo ordena."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.li3"
msgid "World projects are built by everyone. Any citizen can contribute."
msgstr "Los proyectos del mundo los construyen todos. Cualquier ciudadano puede contribuir."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.li4"
msgid "Upgrades and world projects earn a country prestige."
msgstr "Las mejoras y los proyectos del mundo dan prestigio a un país."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.line"
msgid "Roads, industry, research and world projects."
msgstr "Carreteras, industria, investigación y proyectos del mundo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.p1"
msgid "Every province has three kinds of infrastructure: transport, industrial and civil, each up to level 10. A country builds them by opening a worksite, by law or by a minister’s order, and its citizens build it shift by shift, paid from the treasury."
msgstr "Cada provincia tiene tres tipos de infraestructura: de transporte, industrial y civil, cada una hasta el nivel 10. Un país las construye abriendo una obra, por ley o por orden de un ministro, y sus ciudadanos la construyen turno a turno, con pago del tesoro público."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.development.title"
msgid "Roads, research and world projects"
msgstr "Carreteras, investigación y proyectos del mundo"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.line"
msgid "Running, voting, and asking the country one question."
msgstr "Presentarse, votar y hacer una pregunta al país."

#. {nominationDays} is a number of days. {votingDays} is a number of days.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.p1"
msgid "<b>An election fills an office or the chamber’s seats. Candidates have {nominationDays} day to run, then voting is open for {votingDays} day. Your vote is secret.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Una elección cubre un cargo o los escaños de la cámara. Los candidatos tienen {nominationDays} día para presentarse y luego la votación está abierta {votingDays} día. Tu voto es secreto.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.p2"
msgid "If nobody runs against you, you take the seat when entries close, with no vote."
msgstr "Si nadie se presenta contra ti, te quedas con el puesto cuando se cierran las candidaturas, sin votación."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.p3"
msgid "A referendum asks every citizen one question. It opens at once and runs for {hours} hours. Its answer binds nobody: acting on it is up to the government."
msgstr "Un referendo hace una pregunta a todos los ciudadanos. Se abre de inmediato y dura {hours} horas. Su resultado no obliga a nadie: actuar según él depende del gobierno."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.p4"
msgid "To vote: open Country, Politics, Elections, then the election, then Vote. You can vote once you have been a citizen long enough; the screen shows your date."
msgstr "Para votar: abre País, Política, Elecciones, luego la elección y luego Votar. Puedes votar cuando lleves suficiente tiempo con la ciudadanía; la pantalla muestra tu fecha."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.p5"
msgid "To run: the same election, Run for this office. You can choose a party to run for."
msgstr "Para presentarte: en la misma elección, Presentarse a este cargo. Puedes elegir un partido por el que presentarte."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.p6"
msgid "Words: Candidate: somebody running. Ballot: the list you vote on."
msgstr "Palabras: Candidato: alguien que se presenta. Boleta: la lista en la que votas."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.elections.title"
msgid "How do elections and referendums work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan las elecciones y los referendos?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.after"
msgid "With too little Energy, an act waits until you have enough. Nothing else happens to you."
msgstr "Con muy poca Energía, una acción espera hasta que tengas suficiente. No te pasa nada más."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.answer"
msgid "Energy is what work, training and fighting spend; it comes back when you eat, and slowly by itself."
msgstr "La Energía es lo que gastan el trabajo, el entrenamiento y el combate; vuelve cuando comes, y despacio por sí sola."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.line"
msgid "What spends it, and how it comes back."
msgstr "Qué la gasta y cómo vuelve."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {shortShift} is an amount of Energy. {fullShift} is an amount of Energy. {training} is an amount of Energy. {energy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.step1.how"
msgid "a short shift costs {shortShift}, a full one {fullShift}, training {training}, and each attack in a battle {energy}."
msgstr "un turno corto cuesta {shortShift}, uno completo {fullShift}, el entrenamiento {training} y cada ataque en una batalla {energy}."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.step1.to"
msgid "To know what it costs"
msgstr "Para saber cuánto cuesta"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {foodEnergy} is an amount of Energy. {maxEnergy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.step2.how"
msgid "press Eat. One food gives {foodEnergy} Energy, up to {maxEnergy}."
msgstr "pulsa Comer. Una comida da {foodEnergy} de Energía, hasta {maxEnergy}."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.step2.to"
msgid "To get it back"
msgstr "Para recuperarla"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {perHour} is an amount of Energy. {restingEnergy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.step3.how"
msgid "it comes back by itself, {perHour} at the start of every hour, while you have less than {restingEnergy}."
msgstr "vuelve sola, {perHour} al comienzo de cada hora, mientras tengas menos de {restingEnergy}."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.step3.to"
msgid "To wait instead"
msgstr "Para esperar sin comer"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.synonyms"
msgid "energy, tired, rest, resting, food, eat, hungry"
msgstr "energía, energia, cansado, cansancio, descanso, descansar, comida, comer, hambre"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.title"
msgid "How Energy works"
msgstr "Cómo funciona la Energía"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence. {restingEnergy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.word1.means"
msgid "The {restingEnergy} Energy it comes back to by itself."
msgstr "Los {restingEnergy} de Energía hasta los que vuelve sola."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.energy.word1.term"
msgid "Resting level"
msgstr "Nivel de descanso"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.h1"
msgid "What is different"
msgstr "Qué es diferente"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.h2"
msgid "Before the first government"
msgstr "Antes del primer gobierno"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.h3"
msgid "Running unopposed"
msgstr "Presentarse sin oposición"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.line"
msgid "Why the first days in a country are easier."
msgstr "Por qué los primeros días en un país son más fáciles."

#. {companies} is a number of companies. {days} is a number of days.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p1"
msgid "A country is new from the day its first citizen arrives until players own {companies} companies there, or for {days} days, whichever comes first. The Country screen says when yours is."
msgstr "Un país es nuevo desde el día en que llega su primer ciudadano hasta que los jugadores poseen {companies} empresas allí, o durante {days} días, lo que ocurra primero. La pantalla País dice hasta cuándo lo es el tuyo."

#. {newCountryGrant} is the money a newcomer starts with in a country that is still new, drawn as a coin amount. {starterGrant} is the money a new citizen starts with, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p2"
msgid "Newcomers here start with {newCountryGrant} instead of {starterGrant}, and founding a company here needs no waiting, whoever founds it."
msgstr "Quienes llegan aquí empiezan con {newCountryGrant} en lugar de {starterGrant}, y fundar una empresa aquí no requiere espera, la funde quien la funde."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p3"
msgid "If you started playing in that country, you can vote and run for office at once, with no waiting. Somebody who moves there from another country waits the usual time for a newcomer from abroad, new country or not. When the country stops being new, the usual waits come back for everybody, counted from the day each person arrived: somebody who arrived yesterday waits out the rest of theirs, and the Country screen gives them the day."
msgstr "Si empezaste a jugar en ese país, puedes votar y presentarte a un cargo de inmediato, sin esperar. Quien llega desde otro país espera el tiempo habitual de quien viene del extranjero, sea el país nuevo o no. Cuando el país deja de ser nuevo, las esperas habituales vuelven para todos, contadas desde el día en que llegó cada persona: quien llegó ayer cumple el resto de la suya, y la pantalla País le da el día."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p4"
msgid "Until somebody is elected, nobody governs. What runs on its own keeps running, and nobody can pass a law, spend from the treasury or declare war. A monarchy with nobody on its throne holds a first election for it among its citizens, and whoever wins holds it for life."
msgstr "Hasta que alguien es elegido, nadie gobierna. Lo que funciona solo sigue funcionando, y nadie puede aprobar una ley, gastar del tesoro público ni declarar la guerra. Una monarquía sin nadie en el trono celebra una primera elección para él entre sus ciudadanos, y quien gana lo ocupa de por vida."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p5"
msgid "If nobody runs against you, there is nothing to vote on: when entries close, you take the seat. So if you are the only one running for President, you become President. A chamber is elected by place, so for a seat in it that means nobody else running where you live. A name on a ballot cannot be taken off, and the Run button says so before you press it. An office the chamber chooses is never taken unopposed: its members vote even when one person runs."
msgstr "Si nadie se presenta contra ti, no hay nada que votar: cuando se cierran las candidaturas, te quedas con el puesto. Así, si eres la única persona que se presenta a la presidencia, la ocupas. Una cámara se elige por lugar, así que para un escaño en ella eso significa que nadie más se presenta donde vives. Un nombre en una boleta no se puede quitar, y el botón Presentarse lo dice antes de que lo pulses. Un cargo que elige la cámara nunca se obtiene sin oposición: sus miembros votan aunque se presente una sola persona."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.title"
msgid "A new country"
msgstr "Un país nuevo"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.line"
msgid "Where a government speaks for its country."
msgstr "Donde un gobierno habla en nombre de su país."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.p1"
msgid "<b>It is where a government speaks for its country.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Es donde un gobierno habla en nombre de su país.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.p2"
msgid "To read it: its notices appear in News under Your country, marked Official notice, and its front page lists all of them and the offices that write there. Every citizen of the country gets its notices without following it."
msgstr "Para leerlo: sus avisos aparecen en Noticias, en Tu país, marcados como Aviso oficial, y su portada los lista todos junto con los cargos que escriben allí. Todos los ciudadanos del país reciben sus avisos sin seguirlo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.p3"
msgid "To write a notice: hold an office that writes there, then press Write a notice on its front page. A notice costs nothing to print, and you write it while you hold the office."
msgstr "Para escribir un aviso: ocupa un cargo que escriba allí y luego pulsa Escribir un aviso en su portada. Un aviso no cuesta nada imprimirlo, y lo escribes mientras ocupas el cargo."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.title"
msgid "What is the Official Gazette?"
msgstr "¿Qué es el Boletín Oficial?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.line"
msgid "Give goods to a person, or offer them for a price."
msgstr "Da bienes a una persona u ofrécelos por un precio."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p1"
msgid "<b>Open their page and press Give or sell, or start from a good in your Inventory.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Abre su página y pulsa Dar o vender, o empieza desde un bien de tu Inventario.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p2"
msgid "To give: choose Give, what and how many, and press Give. To sell: choose Sell and set a price for all of it, which they pay when they accept."
msgstr "Para dar: elige Dar, qué y cuántos, y pulsa Dar. Para vender: elige Vender y fija un precio por todo, que la persona paga cuando acepta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p3"
msgid "What you send is held for them at once, and they are told. If they say no, or do not answer in time, it all comes back to you. You can withdraw the offer before they answer."
msgstr "Lo que envías queda retenido para esa persona de inmediato, y se le avisa. Si dice que no, o no responde a tiempo, todo vuelve a ti. Puedes retirar la oferta antes de que responda."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p4"
msgid "Goods given or sold to a person pay no freight and no import tax, wherever they are."
msgstr "Los bienes dados o vendidos a una persona no pagan flete ni impuesto a la importación, esté donde esté."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p5"
msgid "For your first {hours} hours, your starting gear and early rewards cannot be sold or given away. The sheet says the day you can."
msgstr "Durante tus primeras {hours} horas, tu equipo inicial y tus primeras recompensas no se pueden vender ni regalar. El panel dice el día en que podrás."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p6"
msgid "Words: Held: kept for them until they answer."
msgstr "Palabras: Retenido: guardado para esa persona hasta que responda."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.title"
msgid "How do I give or sell to someone?"
msgstr "¿Cómo doy o vendo algo a alguien?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.line"
msgid "Telling your side where to fight."
msgstr "Decirle a tu bando dónde combatir."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.p1"
msgid "An order is given on a battle, in the name of a unit (by its commander or an officer) or of a country (by whoever holds that power). It says what to do, how urgent it is and when it ends."
msgstr "Una orden se da sobre una batalla, en nombre de una unidad (por su comandante o un oficial) o de un país (por quien tenga esa facultad). Dice qué hacer, qué tan urgente es y cuándo termina."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.p2"
msgid "Everybody fighting for your side in that battle reads it right above the Fight buttons, and the unit’s soldiers see it first in Now. Other orders keep standing beside it. Whoever gave an order can take it back while it stands, and it ends by itself when its time is up or its battle is decided."
msgstr "Quienes combaten por tu bando en esa batalla la leen justo encima de los botones Combatir, y los soldados de la unidad la ven primero en Ahora. Las otras órdenes siguen vigentes a su lado. Quien dio una orden puede retirarla mientras esté vigente, y termina sola cuando se acaba su plazo o se decide su batalla."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.title"
msgid "Giving orders"
msgstr "Dar órdenes"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.line"
msgid "Gear, food, goods and cases."
msgstr "Equipo, comida, bienes y cajas."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p1"
msgid "<b>Inventory holds what you wear, your goods and your cases. What a company or a unit you run holds is on its own page.</b>"
msgstr "<b>El Inventario guarda lo que llevas puesto, tus bienes y tus cajas. Lo que guarda una empresa o una unidad que diriges está en su propia página.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p2"
msgid "To wear something: press Wear on a piece. You wear five: a weapon, a helmet, body armor, legwear and boots. Power is how hard you hit, Protection how much of a hit your armor takes, and Mobility how light you move."
msgstr "Para ponerte algo: pulsa Ponerse en una pieza. Llevas cinco: un arma, un casco, una armadura, pantalones y botas. Fuerza es cuánto golpeas, Protección cuánto de un golpe absorbe tu armadura y Movilidad qué tan ligero te mueves."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p3"
msgid "To mend a piece: open it and press Repair, which costs Scrap. A piece at nothing is broken and stops counting in a fight. Only a broken piece can be broken up for Scrap or retired."
msgstr "Para reparar una pieza: ábrela y pulsa Reparar, que cuesta Chatarra. Una pieza a cero está rota y deja de contar en un combate. Solo una pieza rota se puede desmontar para obtener Chatarra o dar de baja."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p4"
msgid "To use goods: open one to sell it, give it to someone, or, for food, eat it. To open a case: press Open one, or Open all."
msgstr "Para usar bienes: abre uno para venderlo, dárselo a alguien o, si es comida, comerlo. Para abrir una caja: pulsa Abrir una caja o Abrir todas."

#. {common} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {uncommon} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {rare} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {epic} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {legendary} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p5"
msgid "Gear made in a factory comes out rarer than gear from a case: {common}% Common, {uncommon}% Uncommon, {rare}% Rare, {epic}% Epic and {legendary}% Legendary."
msgstr "El equipo fabricado en una fábrica tiene mayor rareza que el de una caja: {common}% Común, {uncommon}% Poco común, {rare}% Raro, {epic}% Épico y {legendary}% Legendario."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p6"
msgid "Words: Scrap: what gear is mended with. Condition: how worn a piece is, out of the best it can still reach."
msgstr "Palabras: Chatarra: con lo que se repara el equipo. Estado: cuánto desgaste tiene una pieza, sobre lo mejor que aún puede alcanzar."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.title"
msgid "What do I own, and how do I use it?"
msgstr "¿Qué tengo y cómo lo uso?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.after"
msgid "You hold one job at a time. Taking one withdraws your other applications."
msgstr "Tienes un solo empleo a la vez. Aceptar uno retira tus otras solicitudes."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.answer"
msgid "Apply for a job and work its shifts; for {hours} hours after you are hired, neither you nor the company can end it."
msgstr "Solicita un empleo y trabaja sus turnos; durante {hours} horas tras la contratación, ni tú ni la empresa pueden terminarlo."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.line"
msgid "Applying, working and leaving."
msgstr "Solicitar, trabajar y dejar el empleo."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step1.how"
msgid "open Ways to earn, then Jobs. Some jobs hire you at once; others send your application to the company, which says yes or no."
msgstr "abre Formas de ganar y luego Empleos. Algunos empleos te contratan de inmediato; otros envían tu solicitud a la empresa, que dice sí o no."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step1.to"
msgid "To apply"
msgstr "Para solicitar"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step2.how"
msgid "each job says what a full and a short shift pay you after tax."
msgstr "cada empleo dice cuánto te paga un turno completo y uno corto después de impuestos."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step2.to"
msgid "To compare"
msgstr "Para comparar"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step3.how"
msgid "your applications are above the board, each with Withdraw it."
msgstr "tus solicitudes están encima del tablero, cada una con Retirarla."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step3.to"
msgid "To change your mind"
msgstr "Para cambiar de opinión"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step4.how"
msgid "press Leave this job on your job's card, once your hours are up."
msgstr "pulsa Dejar este empleo en la tarjeta de tu empleo, cuando se cumplan tus horas."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step4.to"
msgid "To leave"
msgstr "Para dejarlo"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.synonyms"
msgid "job, apply, hire, employer, quit, leave, resign"
msgstr "empleo, trabajo, trabajar, solicitar, postular, postularse, contratar, empleador, renunciar, dejar, abandonar, puesto"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.title"
msgid "How do jobs work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan los empleos?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word1.means"
msgid "What a shift pays before tax."
msgstr "Lo que paga un turno antes de impuestos."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word1.term"
msgid "Wage"
msgstr "Salario"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word2.means"
msgid "A company your country owns; it hires anyone at its wage."
msgstr "Una empresa que posee tu país; contrata a cualquiera con su salario."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word2.term"
msgid "State company"
msgstr "Empresa estatal"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.line"
msgid "What readers send a piece and its writer."
msgstr "Lo que los lectores envían a un artículo y a su redactor."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p1"
msgid "<b>Under every piece, readers write letters and can thank the writer with a tip.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Debajo de cada artículo, los lectores escriben cartas y pueden agradecer al redactor con una propina.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p2"
msgid "To write a letter: type it in the box under the piece and post it. Letters are public, with your name and country. You can withdraw your own letter from its ⋯."
msgstr "Para escribir una carta: escríbela en el cuadro bajo el artículo y publícala. Las cartas son públicas, con tu nombre y tu país. Puedes retirar tu propia carta desde su ⋯."

#. {paperShare} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {minimumTip} is the smallest tip, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p3"
msgid "To thank the writer: press Thank and choose an amount, from {minimumTip}. The writer keeps most of it and the paper keeps the rest ({paperShare}% unless its owner changes it). You thank a writer once for each piece."
msgstr "Para agradecer al redactor: pulsa Agradecer y elige una cantidad, desde {minimumTip}. El redactor se queda con la mayor parte y el periódico con el resto ({paperShare}% salvo que su dueño lo cambie). Agradeces a un redactor una vez por cada artículo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p4"
msgid "To say what you thought: Good piece or Not for me. To report a letter or a piece, open its ⋯."
msgstr "Para decir qué te pareció: Buen artículo o No es para mí. Para denunciar una carta o un artículo, abre su ⋯."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.title"
msgid "How do letters and tips work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan las cartas y las propinas?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.line"
msgid "Buying, selling, and what a trade costs."
msgstr "Comprar, vender y cuánto cuesta una operación."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p1"
msgid "<b>Every good has a page in the Market, with its price delivered to where you are and one button that buys or sells.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Cada bien tiene una página en el Mercado, con su precio puesto en destino hasta donde estás y un botón que compra o vende.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p2"
msgid "To buy: open the good, choose Buy and how many, and press the button. It shows the total, and that is what you pay. The cheapest offers are taken first."
msgstr "Para comprar: abre el bien, elige Comprar y cuántos, y pulsa el botón. Muestra el total, y eso es lo que pagas. Las ofertas más baratas se toman primero."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p3"
msgid "To sell: choose Sell. Sell now sells to the buyers paying most; when nobody is buying, set your own price."
msgstr "Para vender: elige Vender. Vender ahora vende a quienes más pagan; cuando nadie compra, pon tu propio precio."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p4"
msgid "To set your own price: press Set your own price. An offer to buy sets its money aside and a listing holds your goods, until one is taken."
msgstr "Para poner tu propio precio: pulsa Pon tu propio precio. Una oferta de compra aparta su dinero y un anuncio retiene tus bienes, hasta que otra persona acepta."

#. {percent} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {amount} is the size of a trade that asks first, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p5"
msgid "The total is the price, freight by weight and distance, a fee of {percent}% paid to the country the goods are delivered to, and an import tax on goods from another country. A trade of {amount} or more asks you first."
msgstr "El total es el precio, el flete por peso y distancia, una comisión de {percent}% que se paga al país al que se entregan los bienes, y un impuesto a la importación sobre los bienes de otro país. Una operación de {amount} o más te pregunta antes."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p6"
msgid "Until a country’s players make enough, the game’s shop sells food, construction materials, industrial components and fuel in its capital, at a price anyone who makes it can sell for less."
msgstr "Hasta que los jugadores de un país produzcan lo suficiente, la tienda del juego vende comida, materiales de construcción, componentes industriales y combustible en su capital, a un precio que quien lo produzca puede superar vendiendo más barato."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p7"
msgid "Words: Delivered: the price with every charge, to where you are. Bid: an offer to buy at your own price."
msgstr "Palabras: Puesto en destino: el precio con todos los cargos, hasta donde estás. Oferta de compra: una oferta para comprar a tu propio precio."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.title"
msgid "How do I buy and sell?"
msgstr "¿Cómo compro y vendo?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.answer"
msgid "Read the report, decide it within 24 hours, and check the words the player will read before you send them."
msgstr "Lee la denuncia, resuélvela en 24 horas y revisa las palabras que leerá el jugador antes de enviarlas."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.line"
msgid "For staff: the queue, a decision, and an appeal."
msgstr "Para el equipo: la cola, una decisión y una apelación."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step1.how"
msgid "open the staff console: reports are oldest first, and one waiting more than 24 hours says Late."
msgstr "abre la consola del equipo: las denuncias van de la más antigua a la más nueva, y una que lleva más de 24 horas esperando dice Con retraso."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step1.to"
msgid "To see what waits"
msgstr "Para ver qué espera"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step2.how"
msgid "open a report, press Decide, and choose what it stops and for how long."
msgstr "abre una denuncia, pulsa Decidir y elige qué se detiene y por cuánto tiempo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step2.to"
msgid "To decide"
msgstr "Para decidir"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step3.how"
msgid "the question shows the player's sentence, who is told, and that they may appeal."
msgstr "la pregunta muestra la frase que leerá el jugador, a quién se avisa y que puede apelar."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step3.to"
msgid "To check the words"
msgstr "Para revisar las palabras"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step4.how"
msgid "press Nothing was wrong. Close it."
msgstr "pulsa No había ningún problema. Cerrarla."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step4.to"
msgid "To close one with nothing wrong"
msgstr "Para cerrar una sin ningún problema"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step5.how"
msgid "a moderator who did not decide it reads it, and presses Lift it or Keep it."
msgstr "un moderador que no la decidió la lee y pulsa Levantarla o Mantenerla."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step5.to"
msgid "To answer an appeal"
msgstr "Para responder a una apelación"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.synonyms"
msgid "report, sanction, moderate, moderation, appeal, staff"
msgstr "denuncia, denunciar, sanción, sancion, moderar, moderación, moderacion, apelación, apelacion, apelar, equipo, staff"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.title"
msgid "Deciding a report"
msgstr "Resolver una denuncia"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.word1.means"
msgid "A report waiting more than 24 hours."
msgstr "Una denuncia que lleva esperando más de 24 horas."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.word1.term"
msgid "Late"
msgstr "Con retraso"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.word2.means"
msgid "What a decision stops a player doing, and until when."
msgstr "Lo que una decisión impide hacer a un jugador, y hasta cuándo."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.word2.term"
msgid "Sanction"
msgstr "Sanción"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.line"
msgid "CR, what you earn and spend, and where it went."
msgstr "CR, lo que ganas y gastas, y a dónde fue."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p1"
msgid "<b>CR is the money of the world: you earn it, spend it and keep it in your wallet, and every movement is in your Records.</b>"
msgstr "<b>CR es el dinero del mundo: lo ganas, lo gastas y lo guardas en tu billetera, y cada movimiento queda en tus Registros.</b>"

#. {starterGrant} is the money a new citizen starts with, drawn as a coin amount. {newCountryGrant} is the money a newcomer starts with in a country that is still new, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p2"
msgid "To earn it: work a shift for a wage, sell on the Market, or take tips for what you write. New citizens start with {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} in a country that is still new)."
msgstr "Para ganarlo: trabaja un turno por un salario, vende en el Mercado o recibe propinas por lo que escribes. Los ciudadanos nuevos empiezan con {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} en un país que aún es nuevo)."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p3"
msgid "To spend it: buy goods, travel, or start a company, a paper or a bank. An offer to buy sets its money aside: it is still yours, but you cannot spend it until the offer fills or you take it back."
msgstr "Para gastarlo: compra bienes, viaja o funda una empresa, un periódico o un banco. Una oferta de compra aparta su dinero: sigue siendo tuyo, pero no puedes gastarlo hasta que la oferta se cumpla o la retires."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p4"
msgid "To see where it went: open Records at the foot of Money, and choose Earned, Spent, Banks and loans or Trades."
msgstr "Para ver a dónde fue: abre Registros al final de Dinero y elige Ganado, Gastado, Bancos y préstamos u Operaciones."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p5"
msgid "Your country sets its taxes by law, and a new rate starts {hours} hours after the law passes. Its rates are under Country, Economy."
msgstr "Tu país fija sus impuestos por ley, y una tasa nueva empieza {hours} horas después de que se apruebe la ley. Sus tasas están en País, Economía."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p6"
msgid "Words: CR: credits, the game’s money. Set aside: held by an offer to buy, and still yours."
msgstr "Palabras: CR: créditos, el dinero del juego. Apartado: retenido por una oferta de compra, y aún tuyo."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.title"
msgid "How does money work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funciona el dinero?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.after"
msgid "Old links still work: they open the place where the thing lives now."
msgstr "Los enlaces antiguos siguen funcionando: abren el lugar donde está ahora lo que buscabas."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.answer"
msgid "Everything now lives in six places: Home, Market, News, Chat, Country and You. Each place you knew before is inside one of them."
msgstr "Todo está ahora en seis lugares: Inicio, Mercado, Noticias, Chat, País y Tú. Cada lugar que conocías está dentro de uno de ellos."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.line"
msgid "Where Today, Work, Press, Banking and the Menu went."
msgstr "Dónde fueron Hoy, Trabajo, Prensa, Banca y el Menú."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step1.how"
msgid "press Home. Now and Today hold your next steps, your shift, training and eating. Jobs is under Find a job."
msgstr "pulsa Inicio. Ahora y Hoy reúnen tus próximos pasos, tu turno, el entrenamiento y la comida. Empleos está en Buscar empleo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step1.to"
msgid "To find Today and Work"
msgstr "Para encontrar Hoy y Trabajo"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step2.how"
msgid "press News: your country's papers, the world's, and the ones you follow."
msgstr "pulsa Noticias: los periódicos de tu país, los del mundo y los que sigues."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step2.to"
msgid "To find Press"
msgstr "Para encontrar Prensa"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step3.how"
msgid "press You, then Money: your accounts, loans and shares. A bank you run is in You too."
msgstr "pulsa Tú y luego Dinero: tus cuentas, préstamos y acciones. Un banco que diriges también está en Tú."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step3.to"
msgid "To find Banking"
msgstr "Para encontrar Banca"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step4.how"
msgid "press Country, then Economy: public works and research."
msgstr "pulsa País y luego Economía: obras públicas e investigación."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step4.to"
msgid "To find Development"
msgstr "Para encontrar Desarrollo"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step5.how"
msgid "press You: what you hold and run, Settings and Help."
msgstr "pulsa Tú: lo que tienes y diriges, Ajustes y Ayuda."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step5.to"
msgid "To find the Menu"
msgstr "Para encontrar el Menú"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.synonyms"
msgid "moved, where is, where did, today, work, press, banking, development, menu, dock, old, changed"
msgstr "movido, mudado, cambió, cambio, cambiado, dónde está, donde esta, dónde quedó, donde quedo, hoy, trabajo, prensa, banca, banco, desarrollo, menú, menu, barra, antiguo, viejo"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.title"
msgid "Where did things move?"
msgstr "¿Dónde quedó cada cosa?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.word1.means"
msgid "One of the six: Home, Market, News, Country and You at the bottom of a phone, with Chat at its top; all six down the side of a desktop."
msgstr "Uno de los seis: Inicio, Mercado, Noticias, País y Tú abajo en un teléfono, con Chat arriba; los seis a un lado en un dispositivo de escritorio."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.word1.term"
msgid "Place"
msgstr "Lugar"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.line"
msgid "A paper's pieces, its writers and its printing money."
msgstr "Los artículos de un periódico, sus redactores y su dinero de impresión."

#. {level} is a player level.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p1"
msgid "<b>Start one from You › Start something once you reach Level {level}.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Crea uno desde Tú › Crear algo cuando llegues al nivel {level}.</b>"

#. {creationFee} is the cost to start a paper, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p2"
msgid "To start it: give it a name and the country it prints from. It costs {creationFee}, which becomes its printing money. A citizen runs one paper at a time."
msgstr "Para crearlo: ponle un nombre y el país desde el que se imprime. Cuesta {creationFee}, que pasa a ser su dinero de impresión. Un ciudadano dirige un periódico a la vez."

#. {printFee} is the cost to print one piece, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p3"
msgid "To publish: each piece costs the paper {printFee} to print. Add money under More options when it runs low."
msgstr "Para publicar: imprimir cada artículo cuesta {printFee} al periódico. Añade dinero en Más opciones cuando le quede poco."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p4"
msgid "To take writers on: invite them from Writers, or accept those who ask. An editor publishes too; a writer sends you their pieces. What writers keep of a tip is yours to set, under More options."
msgstr "Para incorporar redactores: invítalos desde Redactores o acepta a quienes lo pidan. Un editor también publica; un redactor te envía sus artículos. Lo que los redactores se quedan de una propina lo decides tú, en Más opciones."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.title"
msgid "How do I run a newspaper?"
msgstr "¿Cómo dirijo un periódico?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.line"
msgid "Its offices, who holds them, and what each may do."
msgstr "Sus cargos, quién los ocupa y qué puede hacer cada uno."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p1"
msgid "<b>The players holding its offices: a head of state, a head of government, ministers and the members of the chamber.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Quienes ocupan sus cargos: la jefatura de Estado, la jefatura de gobierno, los ministros y los miembros de la cámara.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p2"
msgid "The constitution sets which offices exist and how each is filled: by election, by the chamber, or by an office that appoints to it."
msgstr "La constitución fija qué cargos existen y cómo se cubre cada uno: por elección, por la cámara o por un cargo que nombra a quien lo ocupa."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p3"
msgid "Each office’s page says how it is filled, how long a term lasts and what it may do, each power a door to where it is used."
msgstr "La página de cada cargo dice cómo se cubre, cuánto dura un mandato y qué puede hacer, y cada facultad lleva al lugar donde se usa."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p4"
msgid "To see who holds what: Country, Politics, Offices. An office nobody holds says how it can be filled."
msgstr "Para ver quién ocupa qué: País, Política, Cargos. Un cargo que nadie ocupa dice cómo puede cubrirse."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p5"
msgid "If you hold one, its console is under You: what waits on it first, then what it may do."
msgstr "Si ocupas uno, su consola está en Tú: primero lo que le espera, luego lo que puede hacer."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.title"
msgid "Who runs a country?"
msgstr "¿Quién dirige un país?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.line"
msgid "What you have out on the Market, and what it holds."
msgstr "Lo que tienes en el Mercado y lo que retiene."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p1"
msgid "<b>An order or an offer waits until someone takes it, you take it back, or it ends, and while it waits it holds its money or goods.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Una orden o una oferta espera hasta que alguien la acepta, tú la retiras o termina, y mientras espera retiene su dinero o sus bienes.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p2"
msgid "To see them: open Your orders and offers in the Market. Open lists everything out in your name, what each one holds and when it ends."
msgstr "Para verlas: abre Tus órdenes y ofertas en el Mercado. Abiertas lista todo lo que hay a tu nombre, lo que retiene cada una y cuándo termina."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p3"
msgid "To take one back: press Take back on an order, or Withdraw on an offer you sent. What it held comes back at once."
msgstr "Para retirar una: pulsa Retirar, en una orden o en una oferta que enviaste. Lo que retenía vuelve de inmediato."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p4"
msgid "An order can fill while you are away, when a seller or a buyer meets your price. An offer to a person waits for their answer; if they say no, or do not answer in time, the goods come back."
msgstr "Una orden puede cumplirse mientras estás fuera, cuando un vendedor o un comprador alcanza tu precio. Una oferta a una persona espera su respuesta; si dice que no, o no responde a tiempo, los bienes vuelven."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p5"
msgid "To see what you traded: open Records at the foot. Every closed order and answered offer is there, under its day."
msgstr "Para ver lo que negociaste: abre Registros al final. Cada orden cerrada y cada oferta respondida está ahí, bajo su día."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p6"
msgid "Words: Set aside: money an offer to buy holds, still yours. Held: goods kept for an order or an offer until it ends."
msgstr "Palabras: Apartado: dinero que retiene una oferta de compra, aún tuyo. Retenido: bienes guardados para una orden o una oferta hasta que termina."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.title"
msgid "What happens to my orders and offers?"
msgstr "¿Qué pasa con mis órdenes y ofertas?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.line"
msgid "A group with members and a voice."
msgstr "Un grupo con miembros y voz."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p1"
msgid "<b>A group of players with a name, members and a voice: its leader and officers announce to every member. It has no power in the game.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Un grupo de jugadores con nombre, miembros y voz: su líder y sus autoridades hacen anuncios a todos los miembros. No tiene poder en el juego.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p2"
msgid "To join: open it from Country, People, Organizations. Some let anyone in; others decide each request."
msgstr "Para unirte: ábrela desde País, Personas, Organizaciones. Algunas dejan entrar a cualquiera; otras deciden cada solicitud."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p3"
msgid "To start one: You, Start something. It is free, and you lead it."
msgstr "Para crear una: Tú, Crear algo. Es gratis, y tú la diriges."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p4"
msgid "To leave: on its page, Leave. A leader cannot leave what they lead."
msgstr "Para salir: en su página, Salir. Un líder no puede salir de lo que dirige."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p5"
msgid "Words: Officer: a member who can let people in, remove plain members and announce."
msgstr "Palabras: Autoridad: un miembro que puede admitir personas, expulsar a miembros comunes y hacer anuncios."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.title"
msgid "What is an organization?"
msgstr "¿Qué es una organización?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.line"
msgid "A label candidates share on the ballot."
msgstr "Una etiqueta que comparten los candidatos en la boleta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p1"
msgid "<b>A party is a label candidates share on the ballot. It gives no advantage and holds no power of its own.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Un partido es una etiqueta que comparten los candidatos en la boleta. No da ninguna ventaja y no tiene poder propio.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p2"
msgid "To ask to join: open it from Country, Politics, Parties and press Ask to join. You can ask several parties; you belong to the first that lets you in."
msgstr "Para pedir unirte: ábrelo desde País, Política, Partidos y pulsa Pedir unirse. Puedes pedirlo a varios partidos; perteneces al primero que te admita."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p3"
msgid "To give money: on the party’s page, Money. Every gift is public and cannot be taken back, and the party fund cannot be spent yet."
msgstr "Para dar dinero: en la página del partido, Dinero. Cada donación es pública y no se puede retirar, y el fondo del partido todavía no se puede gastar."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p4"
msgid "To leave: on the party’s page, Leave. When its leader leaves, the party passes to its longest-serving officer."
msgstr "Para salir: en la página del partido, Salir. Cuando su líder se va, el partido pasa a su autoridad con más tiempo en el cargo."

#. {level} is a player level. {fee} is the fee to found a party, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p5"
msgid "To found one: from level {level}, for {fee}, under You, Start something."
msgstr "Para fundar uno: desde el nivel {level}, por {fee}, en Tú, Crear algo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p6"
msgid "Words: Officer: a member who can let people in and remove plain members. Party fund: the money given to a party."
msgstr "Palabras: Autoridad: un miembro que puede admitir personas y expulsar a miembros comunes. Fondo del partido: el dinero que se da a un partido."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.title"
msgid "What is a party for?"
msgstr "¿Para qué sirve un partido?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.line"
msgid "How a war ends."
msgstr "Cómo termina una guerra."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.p1"
msgid "A war ends when one side accepts the other’s peace terms. Terms can hand provinces over and say who keeps what. Whoever holds that power in a country offers them; the other country accepts them, refuses them, or sends different terms back, which take their place."
msgstr "Una guerra termina cuando un bando acepta las condiciones de paz del otro. Las condiciones pueden entregar provincias y decir quién se queda con qué. Quien tiene esa facultad en un país las ofrece; el otro país las acepta, las rechaza o devuelve otras condiciones, que ocupan su lugar."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.p2"
msgid "Terms stand until they are answered or withdrawn. After peace, either country may declare war again."
msgstr "Las condiciones siguen vigentes hasta que se responden o se retiran. Tras la paz, cualquiera de los dos países puede declarar la guerra de nuevo."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.title"
msgid "Peace terms"
msgstr "Condiciones de paz"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.line"
msgid "A citizen's public record."
msgstr "El registro público de un ciudadano."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p1"
msgid "<b>Their public record: who they are and what they have done.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Su registro público: quién es y qué ha hecho.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p2"
msgid "It shows their banner and picture, their name and title, their level and country, where they are, their own words, the seals they chose to show, their statistics and their record. Anyone can read it."
msgstr "Muestra su banner y su imagen, su nombre y título, su nivel y país, dónde está, sus propias palabras, los sellos que eligió mostrar, sus estadísticas y su registro. Cualquiera puede leerla."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p3"
msgid "To change yours: open You, then Your page, and press Edit. Your picture, banner and words are set in Settings. On You, each fact others can also see says Public."
msgstr "Para cambiar la tuya: abre Tú, luego Tu página, y pulsa Editar. Tu imagen, tu banner y tus palabras se fijan en Ajustes. En Tú, cada dato que otros también pueden ver dice Público."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p4"
msgid "To choose the seals on show: in Achievements, turn on Show on my page. You get room for more as you level up."
msgstr "Para elegir los sellos que se muestran: en Logros, activa Mostrar en mi página. Tienes espacio para más a medida que subes de nivel."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.title"
msgid "What does a citizen's page show?"
msgstr "¿Qué muestra la página de un ciudadano?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.line"
msgid "Newspapers written by players."
msgstr "Periódicos escritos por jugadores."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p1"
msgid "<b>News is the papers players write, as headlines you open and read.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Noticias son los periódicos que escriben los jugadores, como titulares que abres y lees.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p2"
msgid "To read: open a headline. A dot marks one you have not opened yet. Your country shows your country’s papers (press its flag to read another country’s), The world shows every paper, and Following shows the papers you follow."
msgstr "Para leer: abre un titular. Un punto marca uno que aún no has abierto. Tu país muestra los periódicos de tu país (pulsa su bandera para leer los de otro país), El mundo muestra todos los periódicos y Siguiendo muestra los periódicos que sigues."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p3"
msgid "To keep up with a paper: press Follow on its front page or under one of its pieces. Its new pieces then come to Following. Pieces you liked are kept there too."
msgstr "Para estar al día con un periódico: pulsa Seguir en su portada o debajo de uno de sus artículos. Sus artículos nuevos llegan entonces a Siguiendo. Los artículos que te gustaron también se guardan allí."

#. {level} is a player level.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p4"
msgid "To write: if you write for a paper, Write is under the tabs. Anyone can start a paper from Level {level}."
msgstr "Para escribir: si escribes para un periódico, Escribir está debajo de las pestañas. Cualquiera puede crear un periódico desde el nivel {level}."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.title"
msgid "How does News work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funciona Noticias?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.line"
msgid "The head of government, and the powers of the office."
msgstr "La jefatura de gobierno y las facultades del cargo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p1"
msgid "<b>A Prime Minister heads the government. What the office may do is set by the country’s constitution and listed on its page.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Un Primer ministro encabeza el gobierno. Lo que puede hacer el cargo lo fija la constitución del país y se lista en su página.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p2"
msgid "Its powers often include appointing ministers, proposing bills and spending from the Treasury up to a limit the law sets. A power the office lacks is shown with who holds it instead."
msgstr "Sus facultades suelen incluir nombrar ministros, proponer proyectos de ley y gastar del tesoro público hasta un límite que fija la ley. Una facultad que el cargo no tiene se muestra con quién la tiene en su lugar."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p3"
msgid "To act: open the office’s console under You. What waits on it comes first, then its powers in groups, each act asking before it is done."
msgstr "Para actuar: abre la consola del cargo en Tú. Primero va lo que le espera y luego sus facultades en grupos, y cada acto pide confirmación antes de hacerse."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p4"
msgid "Words: Head of government: the office that runs the country day to day."
msgstr "Palabras: Jefatura de gobierno: el cargo que dirige el país en el día a día."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.title"
msgid "What does a Prime Minister do?"
msgstr "¿Qué hace un Primer ministro?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.after"
msgid "Wealth shows your position only. No amount of anybody's money is ever shown."
msgstr "La riqueza muestra solo tu posición. Nunca se muestra la cantidad de dinero de nadie."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.answer"
msgid "Rankings count who is ahead this week, this month and for all time; they are for pride and pay nothing."
msgstr "Las clasificaciones cuentan quién va por delante esta semana, este mes y de todos los tiempos; son por orgullo y no pagan nada."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.line"
msgid "Who is ahead, and what the world builds."
msgstr "Quién va por delante y qué construye el mundo."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.step1.how"
msgid "open Rankings from The world: citizens, countries, military units, companies and newspapers, the top 50 of each."
msgstr "abre Clasificaciones desde El mundo: ciudadanos, países, unidades militares, empresas y periódicos, los 50 primeros de cada uno."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.step1.to"
msgid "To see the boards"
msgstr "Para ver las tablas"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.step2.how"
msgid "boards are recounted every hour, and the week starts on Monday at midnight UTC."
msgstr "las tablas se recuentan cada hora, y la semana empieza el lunes a medianoche UTC."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.step2.to"
msgid "To know when they change"
msgstr "Para saber cuándo cambian"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.step3.how"
msgid "open The world: its world projects, its eras and what each country has put in."
msgstr "abre El mundo: sus proyectos del mundo, sus eras y lo que ha aportado cada país."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.step3.to"
msgid "To see what the world builds"
msgstr "Para ver qué construye el mundo"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.synonyms"
msgid "ranking, rankings, leaderboard, top, world project, prestige"
msgstr "clasificación, clasificacion, clasificaciones, ranking, rankings, tabla, mejores, top, proyecto del mundo, prestigio"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.title"
msgid "How do rankings and world projects work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan las clasificaciones y los proyectos del mundo?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.safety.line"
msgid "Hide, block or report somebody."
msgstr "Oculta, bloquea o denuncia a alguien."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.safety.p1"
msgid "<b>From the ⋯ beside their name, or beside anything they wrote.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Desde el ⋯ junto a su nombre, o junto a cualquier cosa que escribió.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.safety.p2"
msgid "To hide them: Hide their posts. Their articles, letters and room posts leave your screens, but not your direct messages. Show them again from Chat › People you know."
msgstr "Para ocultar a una persona: Ocultar sus publicaciones. Sus artículos, cartas y mensajes de sala desaparecen de tus pantallas, pero no tus mensajes directos. Vuelve a mostrarla desde Chat › Personas que conoces."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.safety.p3"
msgid "To block them: they cannot write to you in a direct or group room, and you stop seeing what they write in chat."
msgstr "Para bloquear a alguien: esa persona no puede escribirte en una sala directa o de grupo, y dejas de ver lo que escribe en el chat."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.safety.p4"
msgid "To report: choose Report on a message, a letter, a piece or a person, pick what is wrong and add a note if you like. A moderator reads every report, and nobody is told who reported them."
msgstr "Para denunciar: elige Denunciar en un mensaje, una carta, un artículo o una persona, escoge qué está mal y añade una nota si quieres. Un moderador lee cada denuncia, y a nadie se le dice quién lo denunció."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.safety.title"
msgid "How do I hide or report somebody?"
msgstr "¿Cómo oculto o denuncio a alguien?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.answer"
msgid "Settings holds how you look, what others see, your alerts and sound, how you sign in, and your account."
msgstr "Ajustes guarda tu aspecto, lo que ven los demás, tus avisos y tu sonido, cómo inicias sesión y tu cuenta."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.line"
msgid "How you look, what others see, alerts and your account."
msgstr "Tu aspecto, lo que ven los demás, los avisos y tu cuenta."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step1.how"
msgid "Profile: your picture, banner, words about you and your name."
msgstr "Perfil: tu imagen, tu banner, tus palabras sobre ti y tu nombre."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step1.to"
msgid "To change how you look"
msgstr "Para cambiar tu aspecto"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step2.how"
msgid "Privacy, with the people you hid."
msgstr "Privacidad, con las personas que ocultaste."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step2.to"
msgid "To choose what others see"
msgstr "Para elegir lo que ven los demás"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step3.how"
msgid "Alerts. Language and Sound and radio sit beside it."
msgstr "Avisos. Idioma y Sonido y radio están a su lado."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step3.to"
msgid "To be told on this device"
msgstr "Para recibir avisos en este dispositivo"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step4.how"
msgid "Account and security: your email address, your ways in, your devices, and deleting your account."
msgstr "Cuenta y seguridad: tu correo electrónico, tus formas de entrar, tus dispositivos y la eliminación de tu cuenta."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.settings.step4.to"
msgid "To change how you sign in"
msgstr "Para cambiar cómo inicias sesión"

