#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.line"
msgid "Part of a company you own, and offers to buy or sell some."
msgstr "Una parte de una empresa que posees, y ofertas para comprar o vender algunas."

#. {shares} is a number of shares.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.p1"
msgid "<b>A company is {shares} shares, and more than half of a player’s company is control of it.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Una empresa se divide en {shares} acciones, y tener más de la mitad de las acciones de la empresa de un jugador es tener su control.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.p2"
msgid "Shares change hands only by an offer from one holder to one person, who accepts it or not. There is no share market."
msgstr "Las acciones cambian de manos solo mediante una oferta de un titular a una persona, que la acepta o no. No hay un mercado de acciones."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.p3"
msgid "To answer an offer: it waits in Now and in Money, Shares, with what you pay, for how much of the company, and what you would own after."
msgstr "Para responder a una oferta: espera en Ahora y en Dinero, Acciones, con lo que pagas, por cuánta parte de la empresa y qué poseerías después."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.p4"
msgid "To offer some of yours: open Money, Shares, then Offer shares to someone. Choose who, how many and a price, or no price to give them. Nothing moves until they accept, and you can take it back until then."
msgstr "Para ofrecer algunas tuyas: abre Dinero, Acciones y luego Ofrecer acciones a alguien. Elige a quién, cuántas y un precio, o ningún precio para regalarlas. Nada se mueve hasta que la persona acepta, y puedes retirarla hasta entonces."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.p5"
msgid "To buy from a country: some countries sell shares in their state companies. They are under Shares on offer, and you buy on the company’s page."
msgstr "Para comprar a un país: algunos países venden acciones de sus empresas estatales. Están en Acciones en oferta, y compras en la página de la empresa."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.p6"
msgid "Words: Share: one part of a company. Control: more than half, which lets you run it."
msgstr "Palabras: Acción: una parte de una empresa. Control: más de la mitad, que te permite dirigirla."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.shares.title"
msgid "How do shares work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan las acciones?"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.h1"
msgid "Who runs one"
msgstr "Quién la dirige"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.h2"
msgid "Where the money goes"
msgstr "A dónde va el dinero"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.h3"
msgid "How a country founds, sells and buys one"
msgstr "Cómo un país la funda, la vende y la compra"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.line"
msgid "Companies your country owns, where anyone can work."
msgstr "Empresas que posee tu país, donde cualquiera puede trabajar."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p1"
msgid "Some companies belong to a country rather than a person. They hire, make and sell like any other company, and nothing about them is cheaper or faster. Every country opens with two: a state farm and a state food plant. Both hire anyone at once."
msgstr "Algunas empresas pertenecen a un país y no a una persona. Contratan, producen y venden como cualquier otra empresa, y nada en ellas es más barato ni más rápido. Cada país empieza con dos: una granja estatal y una planta de alimentos estatal. Las dos contratan a cualquiera de inmediato."

#. {day} is a day number of the world's calendar.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p10"
msgid "The companies every country began with can be sold from day {day} of the world."
msgstr "Las empresas con las que empezó cada país se pueden vender desde el Día {day} del mundo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p11"
msgid "Where to find it: a sale is on the company’s own page, in Work → Shares under Companies for sale, and in the country’s Official Gazette."
msgstr "Dónde encontrarla: una venta está en la página de la propia empresa, en Trabajo → Acciones, en Empresas en venta, y en el Boletín Oficial del país."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p2"
msgid "An office of the country runs it, usually the finance minister. Whoever holds that office runs the company for as long as they hold it. They cannot take a job there, raise their own wage there, or trade with it for themselves."
msgstr "Un cargo del país la dirige, normalmente el ministro de Finanzas. Quien ocupa ese cargo dirige la empresa mientras lo ocupe. No puede aceptar un empleo allí, subirse el salario allí ni comerciar con ella por su cuenta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p3"
msgid "When nobody holds the office, the company keeps working on its own: it hires anyone who applies at the wage it already pays, and buys and sells at the going price."
msgstr "Cuando nadie ocupa el cargo, la empresa sigue funcionando sola: contrata a cualquiera que lo solicite con el salario que ya paga, y compra y vende al precio vigente."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p4"
msgid "A state company only offers jobs while it can pay a full shift for every place it has. When it cannot, its jobs disappear from the lists until it has sold enough."
msgstr "Una empresa estatal solo ofrece empleos mientras puede pagar un turno completo por cada puesto que tiene. Cuando no puede, sus empleos desaparecen de las listas hasta que haya vendido lo suficiente."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p5"
msgid "Once a week, what a state company holds beyond two weeks of a full crew’s wages goes to its owners. The country’s share goes into its Treasury, and your country’s Money tab shows what each one last paid."
msgstr "Una vez a la semana, lo que una empresa estatal tiene por encima de dos semanas de salarios de una plantilla completa va a sus propietarios. La parte del país va a su tesoro público, y la pestaña Dinero de tu país muestra lo que pagó cada una la última vez."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p6"
msgid "A country’s chamber can found a state company with money from the Treasury. The bill says what it makes, where its first site stands, and how much it starts with."
msgstr "La cámara de un país puede fundar una empresa estatal con dinero del tesoro público. El proyecto de ley dice qué produce, dónde está su primera instalación y con cuánto empieza."

#. {auctionDays} is a number of days. {offeringDays} is a number of days.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p7"
msgid "A chamber can sell one of the country’s companies in one of two ways. Sealed bids for {auctionDays} days: anyone may bid once, nobody sees another bid, and the highest bid of at least the price the chamber set buys the whole company. Every other bid comes back in full. Or shares at a fixed price for {offeringDays} days, to whoever buys first."
msgstr "Una cámara puede vender una de las empresas del país de dos maneras. Ofertas selladas durante {auctionDays} días: cualquiera puede hacer una oferta una sola vez, nadie ve las ofertas de los demás, y la oferta más alta, de al menos el precio que fijó la cámara, compra la empresa entera. Todas las demás ofertas se devuelven completas. O acciones a un precio fijo durante {offeringDays} días, para quien compre primero."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p8"
msgid "Once the country holds half the shares or fewer, the company is no longer the country’s. Whoever holds the most shares runs it."
msgstr "Cuando el país tiene la mitad de las acciones o menos, la empresa deja de ser del país. Quien tiene más acciones la dirige."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.p9"
msgid "A chamber can buy a company based in its country. Every shareholder is paid for their shares: its sites at today’s building cost and its stock, plus a quarter, and its money, less what it owes. Putting the bill fixes the price. A company that is closing or for sale cannot be bought."
msgstr "Una cámara puede comprar una empresa con sede en su país. Se paga a cada accionista por sus acciones: sus instalaciones al costo de construcción de hoy y sus existencias, más una cuarta parte, y su dinero, menos lo que debe. Proponer el proyecto de ley fija el precio. Una empresa que se está cerrando o está en venta no se puede comprar."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.stateCompanies.title"
msgid "How do state companies work?"
msgstr "¿Cómo funcionan las empresas estatales?"

#. One step of a page: {to} is what the player wants to do, written as the start of a sentence ("To travel"), and {how} is what to do, which begins in lower case in English ("open a province on the map…"). The bold start ends in a colon.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.step"
msgid "<b>{to}:</b> {how}"
msgstr "<b>{to}:</b> {how}"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.after"
msgid "On the way you can trade, write and chat, but you cannot work a shift or fight until you arrive."
msgstr "En el camino puedes comerciar, escribir y chatear, pero no puedes trabajar un turno ni combatir hasta llegar."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.answer"
msgid "You stand in one province and live in one: travel moves where you stand, and once you are there you can live there too."
msgstr "Estás en una provincia y vives en una: viajar cambia dónde estás, y cuando llegas también puedes vivir allí."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.line"
msgid "Journeys, flights and your home."
msgstr "Viajes, vuelos y tu hogar."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {fastest} is a number of minutes. {slowest} is a number of minutes. {cheapest} is the lowest fare, drawn as a coin amount. {cheapestAir} is the lowest air fare, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.step1.how"
msgid "open a province on the map and choose Travel. Overland or by sea takes {fastest} to {slowest} minutes, from {cheapest}; by air, from an airport, from {cheapestAir}."
msgstr "abre una provincia en el mapa y elige Viajar. Por tierra o por mar tarda de {fastest} a {slowest} minutos, desde {cheapest}; por aire, desde un aeropuerto, desde {cheapestAir}."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.step1.to"
msgid "To travel"
msgstr "Para viajar"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {km} is a number of kilometres. {minimumEnergy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.step2.how"
msgid "press Arrive now: 1 Energy for every {km} km still to go (at least {minimumEnergy}), and half the fare again."
msgstr "pulsa Llegar ahora: 1 de Energía por cada {km} km que falten (al menos {minimumEnergy}), más la mitad del pasaje."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.step2.to"
msgid "To arrive at once"
msgstr "Para llegar de inmediato"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.step3.how"
msgid "stand in the province, open it and choose Live here."
msgstr "estando en la provincia, ábrela y elige Vivir aquí."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.step3.to"
msgid "To live somewhere"
msgstr "Para vivir en un lugar"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.synonyms"
msgid "travel, move, journey, fly, flight, live, home, residence, map"
msgstr "viajar, viaje, mudarse, mudanza, trasladarse, volar, vuelo, vivir, hogar, residencia, mapa"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.title"
msgid "How do I travel and where do I live?"
msgstr "¿Cómo viajo y dónde vivo?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.word1.means"
msgid "Where you live, shown on your page."
msgstr "Dónde vives, que se muestra en tu página."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.travel.word1.term"
msgid "Residence"
msgstr "Residencia"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.line"
msgid "Taxes in, public spending out."
msgstr "Impuestos que entran, gasto público que sale."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.p1"
msgid "<b>Taxes fill the Treasury: wages are taxed and the tax is paid into it.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Los impuestos llenan el tesoro público: los salarios pagan impuestos y el impuesto se ingresa en él.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.p2"
msgid "Goods bought from another country can carry a duty the buyer’s country sets. Taxes and duties change by law."
msgstr "Los bienes comprados a otro país pueden llevar un arancel que fija el país del comprador. Los impuestos y los aranceles cambian por ley."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.p3"
msgid "The offices that may spend it do so within the limits the law sets: public works, research, budgets, state aid to another country, and its state companies."
msgstr "Los cargos que pueden gastarlo lo hacen dentro de los límites que fija la ley: obras públicas, investigación, presupuestos, ayuda estatal a otro país y sus empresas estatales."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.p4"
msgid "To see it: Country, Economy shows the Treasury, its last movement, and where each part of it goes."
msgstr "Para verlo: País, Economía muestra el tesoro público, su último movimiento y a dónde va cada parte."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.p5"
msgid "Words: Treasury: a country’s own money. Duty: a tax on goods from abroad."
msgstr "Palabras: Tesoro público: el dinero propio de un país. Arancel: un impuesto sobre bienes del extranjero."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treasury.title"
msgid "Where does the country's money come from and go?"
msgstr "¿De dónde viene el dinero del país y a dónde va?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treaties.line"
msgid "Who comes to your side when you are attacked."
msgstr "Quién viene en tu ayuda cuando te atacan."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treaties.p1"
msgid "A defence pact is a treaty between countries: when one of them is attacked, the others are called on and may enter that war on its side. It is a right and not an obligation. Entering costs nothing, refusing is recorded publicly, and saying nothing is an answer too."
msgstr "Un pacto de defensa es un tratado entre países: cuando uno de ellos es atacado, se llama a los demás y pueden entrar en esa guerra de su lado. Es un derecho y no una obligación. Entrar no cuesta nada, rechazar queda registrado públicamente, y no decir nada también es una respuesta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treaties.p2"
msgid "A treaty is proposed by whoever holds that power and comes into force once each country has agreed, the way its own laws say."
msgstr "Un tratado lo propone quien tiene esa facultad y entra en vigor cuando cada país lo ha aceptado, como dicen sus propias leyes."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.treaties.title"
msgid "Treaties and allies"
msgstr "Tratados y aliados"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.h1"
msgid "Ranks"
msgstr "Rangos"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.h2"
msgid "Treasury and armoury"
msgstr "Tesorería y arsenal"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.h3"
msgid "Machines and the base"
msgstr "Máquinas y la base"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.h4"
msgid "Leaving and disbanding"
msgstr "Salir y disolver"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.line"
msgid "Fighting together under one commander."
msgstr "Combatir juntos bajo un solo comandante."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.p1"
msgid "A military unit is people of one country who fight together. Anyone can start one, free, and command it; a citizen serves in one unit at a time. Its page is public."
msgstr "Una unidad militar es un grupo de personas de un mismo país que combaten juntas. Cualquiera puede crear una, gratis, y comandarla; un ciudadano sirve en una unidad a la vez. Su página es pública."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.p2"
msgid "The commander runs it. Officers give the unit’s orders, answer people who ask to serve and can remove a soldier; if the commander leaves, the unit passes to its longest-serving officer. Soldiers read the orders, stock the armoury and draw on it."
msgstr "El comandante la dirige. Los oficiales dan las órdenes de la unidad, responden a quienes piden servir y pueden expulsar a un soldado; si el comandante se va, la unidad pasa a su oficial más antiguo. Los soldados leen las órdenes, abastecen el arsenal y toman de él."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.p3"
msgid "A unit has no income of its own: its treasury is what members pay in, and nobody can pay it back out to them. Its armoury holds the goods members put in for everyone."
msgstr "Una unidad no tiene ingresos propios: su tesorería es lo que aportan los miembros, y nadie puede devolvérselo. Su arsenal guarda los bienes que los miembros ponen para todos."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.p4"
msgid "A machine the unit holds can be put into service at its base, for a fee from the treasury. It cannot be undone. The base is chosen when the unit starts and moves only if its province is lost, free, by the commander."
msgstr "Una máquina que tiene la unidad se puede poner en servicio en su base, por una tasa de la tesorería. No se puede deshacer. La base se elige cuando se crea la unidad y solo se mueve si se pierde su provincia, gratis, por orden del comandante."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.p5"
msgid "A soldier can leave at any time, free. A unit is disbanded only by its last member, and wound up rather than deleted: its record stays."
msgstr "Un soldado puede salir en cualquier momento, gratis. Una unidad solo la disuelve su último miembro, y se liquida en lugar de borrarse: su registro permanece."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.units.title"
msgid "Units"
msgstr "Unidades"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h1"
msgid "Who can fight"
msgstr "Quién puede combatir"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h2"
msgid "What makes you hit harder"
msgstr "Qué te hace golpear más fuerte"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h3"
msgid "What the ground does"
msgstr "Lo que hace el terreno"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h4"
msgid "What fighting earns"
msgstr "Qué se gana combatiendo"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h5"
msgid "Fighting for pay"
msgstr "Combatir por paga"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h6"
msgid "Machines"
msgstr "Máquinas"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.h7"
msgid "Whose ground"
msgstr "De quién es el terreno"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.li1"
msgid "Citizens of a country in the war, or of its allies."
msgstr "Ciudadanos de un país en la guerra, o de sus aliados."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.li2"
msgid "Anyone, for a side that posts a bounty, and paid for their damage. Never against your own country."
msgstr "Cualquiera, por un bando que publica una recompensa, y se le paga por su daño. Nunca contra tu propio país."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.li3"
msgid "Standing in the battle’s province or one next to it, and not travelling."
msgstr "Estar en la provincia de la batalla o en una vecina, y no estar viajando."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label. {energy} is an amount of Energy.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.li4"
msgid "Each attack costs {energy} Energy."
msgstr "Cada ataque cuesta {energy} de Energía."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.line"
msgid "How battles are fought, and who can fight."
msgstr "Cómo se libran las batallas y quién puede combatir."

#. {rounds} is a number of rounds. {minutes} is a number of minutes.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p1"
msgid "Countries at war fight over provinces. A battle lasts {rounds} rounds of {minutes} minutes. Each round goes to the side that dealt more damage in it, and later rounds count for more. A battle can end early when one side can no longer catch up. A tie goes to extra rounds, and if it is still tied the defender wins."
msgstr "Los países en guerra combaten por las provincias. Una batalla dura {rounds} rondas de {minutes} minutos. Cada ronda la gana el bando que hizo más daño en ella, y las rondas posteriores cuentan más. Una batalla puede terminar antes cuando un bando ya no puede alcanzar al otro. Un empate pasa a rondas extra, y si sigue empatado gana el defensor."

#. {attacks} is a number of attacks. {provinces} is a number of provinces.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p2"
msgid "A country runs one battle at a time against each enemy, and at most {attacks} attacks at once, plus one more for every {provinces} provinces it holds."
msgstr "Un país libra una batalla a la vez contra cada enemigo, y como máximo {attacks} ataques a la vez, más uno por cada {provinces} provincias que controla."

#. {declareDays} is a number of days. {battleDays} is a number of days. {floor} is the lowest price, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p3"
msgid "Declaring a war costs the country’s Treasury {declareDays} days of what it takes in, and opening a battle {battleDays} day, never less than {floor}. War shows today’s price before anybody presses."
msgstr "Declarar una guerra cuesta al tesoro público del país {declareDays} días de lo que ingresa, y abrir una batalla {battleDays} día, nunca menos de {floor}. Guerra muestra el precio de hoy antes de que nadie pulse."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p4"
msgid "Your combat skill, which grows each time you train, and your weapon’s power. Terrain, supply and a little luck change it slightly. Your rank shows what you have done and adds no damage."
msgstr "Tu habilidad de combate, que crece cada vez que entrenas, y la fuerza de tu arma. El terreno, el suministro y un poco de suerte la cambian ligeramente. Tu rango muestra lo que has hecho y no añade daño."

#. {damage} is an amount of damage. {dailyCap} is an amount of XP. {attacks} is a number of attacks.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p5"
msgid "When a battle is decided, everyone who fought in it gets 1 XP for every {damage} damage they dealt, up to {dailyCap} a day, win or lose. The winning side also gets a case for {attacks} attacks or more, one a day. The top fighter on each side gets a medal."
msgstr "Cuando se decide una batalla, todos los que combatieron en ella reciben 1 XP por cada {damage} de daño que hicieron, hasta {dailyCap} al día, ganen o pierdan. El bando ganador también recibe una caja por {attacks} ataques o más, una al día. Quien más daño hizo en cada bando recibe una medalla."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p6"
msgid "When attackers win, their country takes control of the province. Military units are groups of players who fight together; anyone can found one, free."
msgstr "Cuando ganan los atacantes, su país toma el control de la provincia. Las unidades militares son grupos de jugadores que combaten juntos; cualquiera puede fundar una, gratis."

#. {lowest} is the lowest pay, drawn as a coin amount. {highest} is the highest pay, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p7"
msgid "A side can post a bounty: it pays anyone who fights for it, from any country, for the damage they deal, between {lowest} and {highest} per 100 damage, up to the most one fighter can earn, while its budget lasts. You must be in the province or next to it and not travelling, have the Energy for an attack, and not fight against your own country. Once you join a side for pay you keep it for the rest of that battle."
msgstr "Un bando puede publicar una recompensa: paga a cualquiera que combata por él, de cualquier país, por el daño que haga, entre {lowest} y {highest} por cada 100 de daño, hasta lo máximo que puede ganar un combatiente, mientras dure su presupuesto. Debes estar en la provincia o en una vecina y no estar viajando, tener la Energía para un ataque y no combatir contra tu propio país. Una vez que te unes a un bando por paga, te quedas con él el resto de esa batalla."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p8"
msgid "A country and a unit can put machines into service: tanks, artillery and planes. Each is stationed at a base, filled with Fuel from its owner’s stock, and sent to a battle within its reach, where each use spends fuel and wears it down. Bring it home to send it again elsewhere."
msgstr "Un país y una unidad pueden poner máquinas en servicio: tanques, artillería y aviones. Cada una se estaciona en una base, se llena de Combustible de las existencias de su propietario y se envía a una batalla a su alcance, donde cada uso gasta combustible y la desgasta. Hazla volver a su base para enviarla de nuevo a otro lugar."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.p9"
msgid "Holding a province is not owning it. A province’s sheet shows who owns it and, when that is somebody else, who holds it: the owner keeps it on paper and its people stay the owner’s citizens until a peace hands it over. Every country that still claims a province may fight to take it back."
msgstr "Controlar una provincia no es poseerla. La ficha de una provincia muestra a quién pertenece y, cuando es de otro, en manos de quién está: el propietario la conserva sobre el papel y su gente sigue siendo ciudadana de ese país hasta que una paz la entregue. Todo país que aún reclama una provincia puede combatir para recuperarla."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.war.title"
msgid "War and battles"
msgstr "Guerra y batallas"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.answer"
msgid "Work a shift at a job or on public works; a job usually pays more."
msgstr "Trabaja un turno en un empleo o en obras públicas; un empleo suele pagar más."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.line"
msgid "Shifts, public works and jobs."
msgstr "Turnos, obras públicas y empleos."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {shortShift} is an amount of Energy. {fullShift} is an amount of Energy. {times} is how many times the wage a full shift pays.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step1.how"
msgid "press Work a shift on Home, or open Ways to earn. A short shift costs {shortShift} Energy; a full one costs {fullShift}, pays {times} times the wage, and gives your workplace two shifts of work."
msgstr "pulsa Trabajar un turno en Inicio, o abre Formas de ganar. Un turno corto cuesta {shortShift} de Energía; uno completo cuesta {fullShift}, paga {times} veces el salario y da a tu lugar de trabajo dos turnos de trabajo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step1.to"
msgid "To work"
msgstr "Para trabajar"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {wage} is the wage, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step2.how"
msgid "choose public works. A short shift pays {wage} unless your country’s law sets another wage, from the treasury and untaxed."
msgstr "elige obras públicas. Un turno corto paga {wage}, salvo que la ley de tu país fije otro salario, del tesoro público y sin impuestos."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step2.to"
msgid "To work without a job"
msgstr "Para trabajar sin empleo"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step3.how"
msgid "open Ways to earn, then Jobs."
msgstr "abre Formas de ganar y luego Empleos."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step3.to"
msgid "To find a job"
msgstr "Para encontrar un empleo"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step4.how"
msgid "read the pay slip after a shift: the wage, the income tax of the country you work in, and what is yours."
msgstr "lee el recibo de pago después de un turno: el salario, el impuesto sobre la renta del país donde trabajas y lo que es tuyo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.step4.to"
msgid "To see what you kept"
msgstr "Para ver lo que te quedó"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.synonyms"
msgid "job, work, earn, money, wage, pay, shift, worksite, public works"
msgstr "empleo, trabajo, trabajar, ganar, ganar dinero, dinero, salario, sueldo, pago, turno, obra, obras públicas, obras publicas"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.title"
msgid "How do I earn money?"
msgstr "¿Cómo gano dinero?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.word1.means"
msgid "A day's work, once a day."
msgstr "Un día de trabajo, una vez al día."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.word1.term"
msgid "Shift"
msgstr "Turno"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.word2.means"
msgid "Shifts the government pays for, open to anyone."
msgstr "Turnos que paga el gobierno, abiertos a cualquiera."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.word2.term"
msgid "Public works"
msgstr "Obras públicas"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.word3.means"
msgid "A place where a company or a country works."
msgstr "Un lugar donde trabaja una empresa o un país."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.work.word3.term"
msgid "Site"
msgstr "Instalación"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.li1"
msgid "<b>Provinces</b> belong to a country. In a war another country can take one and hold it; the owner still owns it, and the map draws it striped."
msgstr "<b>Las provincias</b> pertenecen a un país. En una guerra otro país puede tomar una y mantenerla; el propietario sigue siéndolo, y el mapa la dibuja a rayas."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.li2"
msgid "<b>An era</b> is a stretch of the world's time. Countries earn prestige in it, and the most prestigious lead the rankings. Nothing about the world resets when an era ends."
msgstr "<b>Una era</b> es un tramo del tiempo del mundo. Los países ganan prestigio en ella, y los de más prestigio lideran las clasificaciones. Nada del mundo se reinicia cuando termina una era."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.li3"
msgid "<b>World projects</b> are built by everybody. Any citizen can give money or goods to one."
msgstr "<b>Los proyectos del mundo</b> los construyen todos. Cualquier ciudadano puede dar dinero o bienes a uno."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.line"
msgid "Its countries, its eras, and what everyone builds together."
msgstr "Sus países, sus eras y lo que todos construyen juntos."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.p1"
msgid "There is one world, and everybody plays in it. It is the real Earth, split into countries and their provinces. Every country is run by its own players, and one with no players yet has every office open."
msgstr "Hay un solo mundo, y todos juegan en él. Es la Tierra real, dividida en países y sus provincias. Cada país lo dirigen sus propios jugadores, y uno que aún no tiene jugadores tiene todos los cargos abiertos."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.p2"
msgid "The world's own page has its rankings, its wars, its projects and every country in it."
msgstr "La página propia del mundo tiene sus clasificaciones, sus guerras, sus proyectos y todos los países que hay en él."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.world.title"
msgid "What is the world?"
msgstr "¿Qué es el mundo?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.writing.line"
msgid "Write for a paper that takes you on."
msgstr "Escribe para un periódico que te incorpore."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.writing.p1"
msgid "<b>Write for a paper that takes you on, or start a paper of your own.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Escribe para un periódico que te incorpore, o crea un periódico propio.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.writing.p2"
msgid "To get a place: a paper’s owner can invite you, and the offer waits in Now. Or press Ask to write here on a paper’s front page, and its owner decides."
msgstr "Para conseguir un puesto: el dueño de un periódico puede invitarte, y la oferta espera en Ahora. O pulsa Pedir escribir aquí en la portada de un periódico, y su dueño decide."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.writing.p3"
msgid "To write: press Write in News, or Write a piece on the paper. When it is ready, press Save and tell the owner. The owner or an editor publishes it, or sends it back with a note; then edit it and send it again."
msgstr "Para escribir: pulsa Escribir en Noticias, o Escribir un artículo en el periódico. Cuando esté listo, pulsa Guardar y avisa al dueño. El dueño o un editor lo publica, o te lo devuelve con una nota; entonces edítalo y envíalo de nuevo."

#. {writerShare} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.writing.p4"
msgid "You keep most of every tip a reader sends you ({writerShare}% unless the owner changes it). To leave, press Stop writing for this paper."
msgstr "Te quedas con la mayor parte de cada propina que te envía un lector ({writerShare}% salvo que el dueño lo cambie). Para salir, pulsa Dejar de escribir para este periódico."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.writing.title"
msgid "How do I write for a paper?"
msgstr "¿Cómo escribo para un periódico?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.you.after"
msgid "A fact that says Public can be read by anyone who opens your page."
msgstr "Un dato que dice Público puede leerlo cualquiera que abra tu página."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.you.answer"
msgid "You is everything that is yours: the places you hold, your money and things, and what you can start."
msgstr "Tú es todo lo que es tuyo: los lugares que ocupas, tu dinero y tus cosas, y lo que puedes crear."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.you.line"
msgid "Your places, what you own, and what you can start."
msgstr "Tus lugares, lo que posees y lo que puedes crear."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.you.step1.how"
